{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie","id":1029643,"title":"Changeling questions from a Newbie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-10T09:57:24-08:00","id":1029643,"title":"Changeling questions from a Newbie","content":"I got quite anumber of questions about the game.<br /> i been dming Demon the Fallen and i learned how to handle both the Demon and The Human host within. which is fairly easy..but what happens when that creature has &quot;Aged.&quot;<br /> What im trying to say is.<br /> Is there a strict relation between the age of the &quot;Host&quot; and the Changeling? will a little kid always be a Childing? or can a little kid be a grump?<br /> <br /> If so, when the human host dies, the changeling reencarnates or he continues with his same current age on a new body?.<br /> <br /> are the Human Host always related to the fae somehow? changeling blood or being replaced on a previous life?<br /> <br /> How does the Experience works out. i dont mean experience points, but rather.. A Changeling is walking on the street, heading to buy some groceries and he suddenly sees a Dragon on the street. people wont see it, but if he fights it (and yes i know that banality would technically kill that dragon), but if the changeling were to fight it.. people would see a normal guy waving his arms with a stick and shouting to the emptiness..right?.<br /> <br /> I noticed that many of the Changelings have certain..Faults or Drawbacks.. must a Pooka ALWAYS Lie (even when he is surrounded by humans and working ?)<br /> <br /> i been dming Mage for a while and i noticed a lot of real mythos between the magicians and the Fae. How does this would work from the point of view of the changelings?.<br /> <br /> Do faes have other realms other than Arcadia that they may arrive to? by the way. i got first edition changeling. so i have no idea if they expanded upon on the second edition.<br /> <br /> also, how doe a changeling feed of Glamour? do they inspire a writter and they tap him on the forehead? do they breath the same air as the person in the room? do they turn his dreams (literally) into liquid or solid foods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-10-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:39:16-08:00","id":1029677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie#post1029643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got quite anumber of questions about the game.<br /> i been dming Demon the Fallen and i learned how to handle both the Demon and The Human host within. which is fairly easy..but what happens when that creature has &quot;Aged.&quot;<br /> What im trying to say is.<br /> Is there a strict relation between the age of the &quot;Host&quot; and the Changeling? will a little kid always be a Childing? or can a little kid be a grump?<br /> <br /> If so, when the human host dies, the changeling reencarnates or he continues with his same current age on a new body?.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of player characters are going to be characters that have undergone the Changeling Way. The Changeling Way isn't body snatching or a faerie wearing a human suit; it's a merging between a faerie soul and a human soul. It results in a unique individual that is neither fully human nor faerie. When the changeling dies, the human half goes on to whatever awaits human souls after death while the fearie half reincarnates by merging with a new unborn human soul. Once that new person's faerie half awakens during her chrysalis, she is new, unique changeling. She might retain some of the memories from her faerie half's previous lives, but she is not a previous changeling reborn. A changeling's life is short, fragile, and incredibly precious.<br /> <br /> The typical exceptions here are the Arcadian sidhe. They take over a human host by displacing the original human soul. However, even for these changelings, their borrowed humanity alters the faerie fundamentally giving them all of their human memories and a more human perspective. Once these changelings die, the faerie within does not reincarnate. No one knows what fate ultimately awaits these faerie souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> are the Human Host always related to the fae somehow? changeling blood or being replaced on a previous life? </div> </div> </div>There is some evidence that faerie souls tend to be drawn more to families that have fae blood within them, but there are plenty of examples of changelings arising in completely mundane families.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does the Experience works out. i dont mean experience points, but rather.. A Changeling is walking on the street, heading to buy some groceries and he suddenly sees a Dragon on the street. people wont see it, but if he fights it (and yes i know that banality would technically kill that dragon), but if the changeling were to fight it.. people would see a normal guy waving his arms with a stick and shouting to the emptiness..right?. </div> </div> </div>The Mists exist to protect the Dreaming from the withering gaze of Banality. For most things that don't directly affect people, the Mists simply hide them. As long as the dragon walking down the street isn't bothering anyone, mundane people will ignore it and subconsciously side step it. For things that are unavoidable, the Mists will alter the person's memories to a mundane explanation.<br /> <br /> The common example is childlings sword fighting with each other look like children playing with sticks to observers. This often gets extrapolated to apply to adult changelings \u2014 adults sword fighting look like they're playing with sticks too, but that's not quite right. The Mists go for a plausible mundane explanation, often piggybacking off the observer's expectations. A group of changelings in a pitched battle on the street corner would more likely be rationalized away as gang violence or rioting after a sports game.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit to add:</b> For some truly outrageous things that can't be rationalized, the Mists just wipe away the memories of ever witnessing them. They'll fade like a poorly remembered dream.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I noticed that many of the Changelings have certain..Faults or Drawbacks.. must a Pooka ALWAYS Lie (even when he is surrounded by humans and working ?) </div> </div> </div>Unless a changeling wants to Invoke the Autumn and invite Banality, she is always bound by her frailties. On the bright side, she always has the benefit of her birthrights as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> i been dming Mage for a while and i noticed a lot of real mythos between the magicians and the Fae. How does this would work from the point of view of the changelings?. </div> </div> </div>What would work best for your chronicle? Go with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do faes have other realms other than Arcadia that they may arrive to? by the way. i got first edition changeling. so i have no idea if they expanded upon on the second edition. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're asking here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also, how doe a changeling feed of Glamour? do they inspire a writter and they tap him on the forehead? do they breath the same air as the person in the room? do they turn his dreams (literally) into liquid or solid foods? </div> </div> </div>I've always imagined it as an energy that changelings absorb making them feel refreshed and vital when they're in the presence of Glamour and worn out and sluggish when Glamour is scarce. There's some cool imagery you've got there though! I could see an unseelie scaring people speechless because she literally eats their words. I'll have to play with that some in future chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-10-2017, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T13:23:08-08:00","id":1029725,"title":"","content":"In the dragon example, if the dragon is attacking, the Mists will help to cover it up. Instead of remembering &quot;a dragon attacked that guy, then his friends drew their swords and tried to slay it,&quot; a mortal might remember &quot;that guy got hit by a garbage truck, then his friends grabbed some crowbars and began bashing it all to hell. This was a weird day.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T18:34:37-08:00","id":1029853,"title":"","content":"The arcadia question: Are there other realms to which the Changeling can access to, besides arcadia and the Dreams?.<br /> Can the Changeling &quot;Teleport&quot; by walking through the dreaming. like entering the dreaming in NY and step out of it on Russia?.<br /> <br /> Is there a correlation between the &quot;Human Host&quot; age and the Changeling age?<br /> <br /> Must the &quot;Changeling self&quot; always co-relate with the body of the host? i mean, Do all Troll's Host's must be Tall and Huge? or can they be a weak looking person ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T18:54:31-08:00","id":1029862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029853#post1029853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arcadia question: Are there other realms to which the Changeling can access to, besides arcadia and the Dreams?.<br /> Can the Changeling &quot;Teleport&quot; by walking through the dreaming. like entering the dreaming in NY and step out of it on Russia?.<br /> <br /> Is there a correlation between the &quot;Human Host&quot; age and the Changeling age?<br /> <br /> Must the &quot;Changeling self&quot; always co-relate with the body of the host? i mean, Do all Troll's Host's must be Tall and Huge? or can they be a weak looking person ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Arcadia question: The Dreaming is filled with interesting locations. I can't recall whether they can cross vast distances quickly through it, though.<br /> <br /> I believe that Seemings have been uncoupled from mortal age for C20, but I think that they were pretty closely related in earlier editions.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the chimerical form needs to perfectly match the physical one, although I do believe that there is some similarity. A troll probably wouldn't look like a pathetic weakling, but an eight-foot tall troll might look like a 6.5 foot tall person to mortals, and seem to duck under things that he shouldn't have needed to in their eyes. Of course, it's easy enough to rule otherwise there, and let the pathetic weakling to shock people with great strength. A satyr would seem to have hairy legs even if they couldn't tell that he was a goat from the waist down. I know that there had been a Wings Merit that required the changeling to be careful with them, even though they were invisible to mortal eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T19:04:36-08:00","id":1029863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029853#post1029853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arcadia question: Are there other realms to which the Changeling can access to, besides arcadia and the Dreams?.<br /> Can the Changeling &quot;Teleport&quot; by walking through the dreaming. like entering the dreaming in NY and step out of it on Russia?.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming is vast and diverse filled with many strange realms. The Near Dreaming roughly parallels the Earth (ala the Penumbra or the Shadowlands) but with manifest dreams and fantasies everywhere; the Far Dreaming is filled with archetypical fantasy realms arranged conceptually; and the Deep Dreaming defies communication.<br /> <br /> Originally the Kithain had no specific access to other realms, though some Gallain that drew Glamour from nature (such as the Nunnehi) accessed the Middle Umbra rather than the Dreaming. Later though, it is a point in the metaplot when the Adhene/Denizens arrive that new Trods appear with them. The &quot;Green Paths&quot; lead into the Middle Umbra. The &quot;Black Paths&quot; lead into the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can travel through the Dreaming to different locations on earth via Trods connecting Freeholds, but it would hardly be &quot;teleportation&quot; given the journey involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T19:48:47-08:00","id":1029876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029853#post1029853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Changeling &quot;Teleport&quot; by walking through the dreaming. like entering the dreaming in NY and step out of it on Russia?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I sort of answered this one in a recent first draft I wrote for an upcoming C20 project. I haven't gotten the redlines back yet, so I don't know if my answer is correct or not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will say though, that it seems to me that the Dreaming's geography would follow dream logic much more than real world physics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a correlation between the &quot;Human Host&quot; age and the Changeling age? </div> </div> </div>This is a hard one for me to answer right now. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> says above, the Seemings are being revised a bit in C20, and I don't want to accidentally spoil anything that hasn't already been spoiled.<br /> <br /> Previous to C20, yes, Seeming was tied closely to the changeling's age (as I said above, &quot;human host&quot; doesn't make much sense when talking about changelings). Childlings were any changeling younger than teenagers. Wilders were teens to about 25 years old. Grumps were any changeling in their late twenties or older.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Must the &quot;Changeling self&quot; always co-relate with the body of the host? i mean, Do all Troll's Host's must be Tall and Huge? or can they be a weak looking person ? </div> </div> </div>Don't think of it as a host. A changeling is a union of a human and faerie soul. It's a single, unique individual that is neither fully human nor completely fae. The Mists obscure the changeling's actual form to mortal eyes, but what mundane sight sees is a plausible rationalization of the changeling's true form. So yeah, a giant towering troll is probably going to appear as a big, imposing due, but within normal human limits.<br /> <br /> That's not to say having a changeling's mortal seeming and fae mein appear totally different is completely out of the question. If it makes for a better story, I'm sure the Dreaming would be all for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-10-2017, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:12:10-08:00","id":1029889,"title":"","content":"Forgot this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029853#post1029853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arcadia question: Are there other realms to which the Changeling can access to, besides arcadia and the Dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the cosmology of Changeling: The Dreaming, there are two major worlds the Kithain deal with \u2014 Earth and the Dreaming. Certain changeling scholars have heard of various other realms that their prodigal cousins interact with, but they tend to view those realms as subsets within one of these two worlds.<br /> <br /> Earth is pretty much the same as the real word, only a little darker, colder, and more hopeless. On the other side of the Mists, the Dreaming is comprised of a nearly infinite number of realms and kingdoms. Some of these realms are merely a passing flight of fancy lasting no more than a single night. Others are permanent fixtures upon the dreamscape that predate the Kithain and their progenitors, the Tuatha de Dannan. The deeper one travels into the Dreaming and farther away one gets from the Banality of Earth, the more fantastic and closer to the old myths the realms of the Dreaming become. At the center of the Dreaming stands Arcadia, the pillar that supports the entirety of the Dreaming and the realm the Kithain claim as their homeland. The gates to Arcadia are lost, obscured by the Mists. None outside Arcadia may enter lest they poison it by their taint of Banality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-10-2017, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:29:05-08:00","id":1029895,"title":"","content":"ok, kind of a silly question: is there a Sandman sort of being, and what other shoutouts can i find to Gaiman on the previous books ? (No C20 to avoid spoilers). any advices when it comes to first edition cantrips?<br /> <br /> is there a way to adapt or evolve cantrips from first, to second, to C20 in an organic way? i mean, im still waiting for second edition to arrive with the mail. but in the mean time my players really want to try out first edition changeling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T21:10:50-08:00","id":1029905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029895#post1029895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, kind of a silly question: is there a Sandman sort of being, and what other shoutouts can i find to Gaiman on the previous books ? (No C20 to avoid spoilers).</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling: The Dreaming has a Gaiman-esque vibe throughout it. It draws pretty heavily on Sandman, Neverwhere, American Gods, and Stardust for inspiration. Even Ocean at the End of the Lane, while written a number of years after Dreaming got canceled, feels like the perfect kinain story. That being said, Changeling doesn't have a Morpheus analog. The closest thing Changeling has to the Endless are the Tuatha de Daanan. They're not a perfect match though. The Tuatha were much more numerous than the Endless. The Tuatha also departed the Dreaming many years ago, leaving their children, the Kithain, as stewards over humanity and the Dreaming in their place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> any advices when it comes to first edition cantrips?<br /> <br /> is there a way to adapt or evolve cantrips from first, to second, to C20 in an organic way? i mean, im still waiting for second edition to arrive with the mail. but in the mean time my players really want to try out first edition changeling </div> </div> </div>The basic structure of cantrips never changed. An Art combines with a Realm while focused through a Bunk to produce an effect. The individual levels of the various Arts changed a bit between editions, as did the levels of the Realms. Bunks were static things you had a list to choose from in first edition while in second edition you were encouraged to make up your own unquie bunks on the fly. First edition cantrips are difficult to use without access to the old cantrip cards. However, if you have access to the Players Guide, it has alternate dice rules for cantrips that should hold you over until you can get ahold of second edition or C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:11:00-08:00","id":1029915,"title":"","content":"In Mage and Demon there's very important laws about &quot;The Naming.&quot; (at least on my Mage game, no PC uses his 'birth name' to protect themselves from Sympathetic Magick. and Demons don't go around revealing their Names so they dont become Slaves). is there anything similar in changeling? or they are Safe if everyone knows that the changeling is &quot;Joe Torien&quot; AKA &quot;Jokah of Roaring Engine Freehold&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:16:02-08:00","id":1029917,"title":"","content":"Also, How married are the changeling's to belief based weaknesses? For example. if i trick a Changeling and force him to make an Oath. he cant break it or use Legal Voids, right?.<br /> <br /> Here in chile we have some fae mythos, for example we have a rapist ogre know as El Trauco. His weakness is that, if you see it and escape from his grasp, he will loose his strenght's and die...<br /> <br /> what im going to is, If people believe in a certain Weakness for the Changeling. does he adopts it? <br /> <br /> also, where can i find more information on the Dreaming as a Realm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T09:08:58-08:00","id":1030082,"title":"","content":"next question: how would an average joe (a lawyer perhaps or a computer IT) suddenly comes to the realization that He is a Changeling? any examples on the &quot;awakening&quot; of a changeling to his/her reality?<br /> <br /> or must all characters be creative or eccentric people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T09:47:11-08:00","id":1030094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1030082#post1030082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">next question: how would an average joe (a lawyer perhaps or a computer IT) suddenly comes to the realization that He is a Changeling? any examples on the &amp;quot;awakening&amp;quot; of a changeling to his/her reality?<br /> <br /> or must all characters be creative or eccentric people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now Crowley, whatever makes you think that a lawyer or computer IT can't be creative or eccentric? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> In seriousness, it really depends on the individual. Generally, I'd say that they'd need to be low in Banality if they're going to be awakening to a fae nature for the first time. They'd probably be especially creative within their fields, if not in their life outside of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:22:29-08:00","id":1030149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1030082#post1030082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">next question: how would an average joe (a lawyer perhaps or a computer IT) suddenly comes to the realization that He is a Changeling? any examples on the &amp;quot;awakening&amp;quot; of a changeling to his/her reality?<br /> <br /> or must all characters be creative or eccentric people?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think that they suddenly realize anything, they are born Changelings, they just slowly enter into the realization that they are not normal over time. A person who becomes a Grump in their thirties probably already lived a life surrounded by the fantastic and, regardless of their profession, would have likely owned thousands of fantasy books, been into tabletop gaming, etc as their Changeling self unconsciously manipulated them into the more comfortable world of fantasy. Unless they have become one of the Autumn People, Changelings will never be considered normal by the people close to then, even before they realized that they were Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:33:02-08:00","id":1030181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1030149#post1030149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not think that they suddenly realize anything, they are born Changelings, they just slowly enter into the realization that they are not normal over time. A person who becomes a Grump in their thirties probably already lived a life surrounded by the fantastic and, regardless of their profession, would have likely owned thousands of fantasy books, been into tabletop gaming, etc as their Changeling self unconsciously manipulated them into the more comfortable world of fantasy. Unless they have become one of the Autumn People, Changelings will never be considered normal by the people close to then, even before they realized that they were Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. A Changeling still undergoes the Chrysalis, which is the awakening of their fae self. Normally this occurs during childhood, but not always. Generally speaking if one has made it to Grump-equivalent age and have yet to undergo their Chrysalis they probably never will, but anything is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:39:02-08:00","id":1030281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029895#post1029895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, kind of a silly question: is there a Sandman sort of being?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Sandman isn't a canon character in Changeling, Dreaming is <b>vast</b> enough to host various creatures from human folklore, some being direct references, others - amalgamations (Dreams &amp; Nighmares and Denizens of the Dreaming, for instance has Norns and Well of Wisdom, Odin himself drank, but no reference of where Odin is now, or even what he is). There might be entire Realms of greek, egyptian, norse and american gods in the Far Dreaming. <i><b>Deep Dreaming</b> </i>is even weirder, than that...<br /> <br /> There may be not Morpheus as cosmic being in Changeling's universe, because it has it's own cosmic beings (Fomorians, Thuatha, etc.), but that doesn't mean, Dreaming can't have creature like Sandman, who think and act in a similar way, even if limited by their respective Realms.<br /> <br /> Or in <i>your Chronicle</i>, someone from Thuatha de Dannan might play such a role. Maybe, Danu, herself. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-11-2017, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:49:24-08:00","id":1030355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029853#post1029853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must the &quot;Changeling self&quot; always co-relate with the body of the host? i mean, Do all Troll's Host's must be Tall and Huge? or can they be a weak looking person ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mentioned, someone in the book, that ignoring chimerical Seeming is big no, for a changeling, that might reward played with a dot of Banality, like Troll getting in a car, he can't fit.<br /> <br /> Which implies, that his Wyrd body might be not as big, as chimerical. Being tall and strong in real life is not unheard of for Trolls, but there's even whole merit, called Huge Size to be as big, as Trolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029917#post1029917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, How married are the changeling's to belief based weaknesses? For example. if i trick a Changeling and force him to make an Oath. he cant break it or use Legal Voids, right?.<br /> <br /> Here in chile we have some fae mythos, for example we have a rapist ogre know as El Trauco. His weakness is that, if you see it and escape from his grasp, he will loose his strenght's and die...<br /> <br /> what im going to is, If people believe in a certain Weakness for the Changeling. does he adopts it?</div> </div> </div> </div>In second edition, usually not. But there is special flaw you can take, that makes changelings vulnerable to various superstitions.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b>, on the other hand, is all about Oaths and how beliefs affect and enslave faerie folk (if they're particularly nasty and harmful), though, it's very different game, set in medieval period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029917#post1029917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, where can i find more information on the Dreaming as a Realm</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Dreams and Nightmares</b> is your book of choice. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-12-2017, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:40:55-08:00","id":1030443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1030355#post1030355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dreams and Nightmares</b> is your book of choice. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Denizens of the Dreaming updates some of D&amp;N's material following the aftermath of the Week of Nightmares, and has some of its own nuggets of info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T07:49:05-08:00","id":1030583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029915#post1029915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Mage and Demon there's very important laws about &quot;The Naming.&quot; (at least on my Mage game, no PC uses his 'birth name' to protect themselves from Sympathetic Magick. and Demons don't go around revealing their Names so they dont become Slaves). is there anything similar in changeling? or they are Safe if everyone knows that the changeling is &quot;Joe Torien&quot; AKA &quot;Jokah of Roaring Engine Freehold&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most changeling have two names they can go by \u2014 their mortal name given to them by their parents and their faerie name that follows them through their reincarnation cycle. Which one they go by most varies from changeling to changeling. Probably due to the Dreaming influencing the parents, a changeling's mortal name and faerie name often sound like variations on the other.<br /> <br /> Everything in Changeling also has an additional true name. This true name is hidden and may change over time as the person or thing it describes changes. Only powerful fae magics can divine something's true name. Once discovered, that same magic may alter the true name, thereby altering whatever it describes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T08:08:31-08:00","id":1030594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029917#post1029917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, How married are the changeling's to belief based weaknesses? For example. if i trick a Changeling and force him to make an Oath. he cant break it or use Legal Voids, right?.<br /> <br /> Here in chile we have some fae mythos, for example we have a rapist ogre know as El Trauco. His weakness is that, if you see it and escape from his grasp, he will loose his strenght's and die...<br /> <br /> what im going to is, If people believe in a certain Weakness for the Changeling. does he adopts it?<br /> <br /> also, where can i find more information on the Dreaming as a Realm</div> </div> </div> </div>Shortly before the Shattering, the fae found themselves being inexplicably affected more and more by human beliefs. At the time, they called these adverse effects Echoes.<br /> <br /> By undergoing the Changeling Way, changelings shield themselves from both Banality and the wild swings in belief and Glamour that result in Echoes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T08:15:40-08:00","id":1030595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1030082#post1030082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">next question: how would an average joe (a lawyer perhaps or a computer IT) suddenly comes to the realization that He is a Changeling? any examples on the &quot;awakening&quot; of a changeling to his/her reality?<br /> <br /> or must all characters be creative or eccentric people?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As others have said, the Glamour within a changeling usually makes her stand out in some way even before her chrysalis. She might not wear loud clothes or be conventionally artist, but she'll probably stand out in her field due to her passion or creative solutions to the problems her career handles. If she becomes too weighed down by Banality, her faerie half might never awaken.<br /> <br /> Also, since when are computer IT folks *not* creative ;P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:26:54-08:00","id":1030652,"title":"","content":"Also, I have a feeling, that even before Chrysalis changelings often feel, like they don't belong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-12-2017, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:56:56-08:00","id":1030704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1030595#post1030595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, since when are computer IT folks *not* creative ;P</div> </div> </div> </div>When you're inevitably given intractable problems to solve with a pittance of resources and manpower you either resign yourself to Banality or you start redefining the laws of your universe and become a substance-fueled philosopher techno-pirate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:45:45-08:00","id":1030762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1030082#post1030082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">next question: how would an average joe (a lawyer perhaps or a computer IT) suddenly comes to the realization that He is a Changeling? any examples on the &quot;awakening&quot; of a changeling to his/her reality?<br /> <br /> or must all characters be creative or eccentric people?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Science and technology is treated with its appropriate creativity levels in C20. Without direct quoting (or referencing, really), I seem to recall the definition being realigned to &quot;whatever bores you out of your mind and feels soul-sucking&quot; is Banal, and &quot;anything that gets you excited and brimming with ideas&quot; is Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:48:07-08:00","id":1030765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029876#post1029876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh, I sort of answered this one in a recent first draft I wrote for an upcoming C20 project. I haven't gotten the redlines back yet, so I don't know if my answer is correct or not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will say though, that it seems to me that the Dreaming's geography would follow dream logic much more than real world physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to me too. Fairy tales and mythology are rife with stepping into the Otherworld and stepping out somewhere that may, or may not, be adjacent to where you originally were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":3785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","user":"Luka C","date":".  basic grammar fail 01-12-2017, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:06:29-08:00","id":1031186,"title":"","content":"any good inspiration for a Chrysalis experience? i mean what triggers it and how would it look like the whole experience of &quot;my life is a lie!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:03:07-08:00","id":1031250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031186#post1031186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any good inspiration for a Chrysalis experience? i mean what triggers it and how would it look like the whole experience of &quot;my life is a lie!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, it's a different game line, but in the first edition of Mage's Cult of Extasy Tradbook there's quite appropraite fiction piece. It's <i>Introduction</i> story, called <b><i>&quot;</i>Fear of Touch<i>&quot;</i></b>. Adjusting for the fact, it's Mages it illustrates the experience of <i>magical awakening</i> very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:28:25-08:00","id":1031265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031186#post1031186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any good inspiration for a Chrysalis experience? i mean what triggers it and how would it look like the whole experience of &quot;my life is a lie!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought of the chrysalis as less a &quot;my life is a lie&quot; moment and more like &quot;this is what my life was always missing.&quot; Glamour is powerful, and even though she hasn't awakened to it yet, it's still called to her for her entire life. It's what always made her the odd one out, the one who sees things a bit differently than anyone else around her. She's probably desperately longed for Glamour even if her conscious mind could never figure out what made her so restless.<br /> <br /> With the chrysalis, she finally becomes whole. All the things that were missing finally fall into place \u2014 things just out of sight that she *knew* where there finally come into focus. Her identity and purpose are finally something she can grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T09:18:23-08:00","id":1031617,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that a Chrysalis doesn't always have to be pleasant. Consider the kind of character being played, and consider sources of inspiration for that character. Matthew Lillard's character from Thirteen Ghosts has the ability to see and feel things other people can't, but it brings him nothing but misery and headaches. The kid from the Sixth Sense is very similar to that. And sometimes, it isn't so much a sense of feeling whole as it is a sense of betrayal. Cypher, from the Matrix, might be a good example of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031265#post1031265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the chrysalis, she finally becomes whole.*</div> </div> </div> </div>*The Dreaming guarantees nothing. Batteries may not be included. No substitutions, exchanges, or refunds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:18:31-08:00","id":1031651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031617#post1031617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that a Chrysalis doesn't always have to be pleasant. Consider the kind of character being played, and consider sources of inspiration for that character. Matthew Lillard's character from Thirteen Ghosts has the ability to see and feel things other people can't, but it brings him nothing but misery and headaches. The kid from the Sixth Sense is very similar to that. And sometimes, it isn't so much a sense of feeling whole as it is a sense of betrayal. Cypher, from the Matrix, might be a good example of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I partially agree with that sentiment, because Unseelie Lagacies tend to be more, well, Unse^W pessimistic.<br /> <br /> World starting to make sense doesn't always mean that the world is a great place, filled with hope and cookies. Changeling finally realizes it's place in that greater tapestry, either it's doing nothing and waiting for inevitable, baking cookies and hope, fighting for the one True King or rebelling against one. <br /> <br /> Or it can be rebellion against their own magical nature, which, if taken to extreme, may result in becoming Dauntain (which isn't the only way, mind you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-14-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:23:10-08:00","id":1031656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031651#post1031651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it can be rebellion against their own magical nature, which, if taken to extreme, may result in becoming Dauntain (which isn't the only way, mind you).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:24:30-08:00","id":1031659,"title":"","content":"@Maggie C<br /> <br /> Um? Did I miss my memo or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:26:36-08:00","id":1031663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031659#post1031659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ummm. Did I miss my memo or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dauntain have been retooled in C20, to be more appropriately thematic than powering their magic through Banality, which is typically the realm of the Autumn People.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:05:04-08:00","id":1031686,"title":"","content":"i was talking to a friend about the Cultural Inheritance in the WoD or the Cultural Feel of each game. Is it normal that most PC's on changeling have Celtic Inheritance? (brit/irish/scottsman etc..)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:06:10-08:00","id":1031690,"title":"","content":"Also, the Dauntain are so damn cool (from an ST perspective, I doubt PCs would agree) now! \ud83d\ude03","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:07:32-08:00","id":1031692,"title":"","content":"Changeling was drawn in part from Celtic mythology, but others, notably satyrs, eshu, trolls, Inanimae, the hsien, the Menehune and the Nunnehi, derive from other mythologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:14:18-08:00","id":1031695,"title":"","content":"Even the sidhe come from different cultures depending on what house they belong to. Aesin and Varich spring to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:18:48-08:00","id":1031699,"title":"","content":"@PookaKnight<br /> Well, Warlocks Dauntain were cool...<br /> <br /> So Autumn People now hold the portfolio of Banality magic powers?<br /> <br /> By the way, I had my theory, based on how it was sometimes described in books, that Banality acts more, like a magical curse rather, than a force entirely opposite of magic. That it's just anti-dreaming magic...<br /> <br /> Something, a salty Fomorian would do. Or an evil artifact of incredible might, used for a good deed, that had nasty side effects. Or Thuatha-de-Dannan themselves <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2014 </span></span>for unknown, mysterious purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 04-23-2017, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:01:13-08:00","id":1031722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031699#post1031699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@PookaKnight<br /> Well, Warlocks Dauntain were cool...<br /> <br /> So Autumn People now hold the portfolio of Banality magic powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Banality kills magic. That's kind of the point. Autumn People have certain abilities derived from Banality, but it's not the same as having Banal magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:03:54-08:00","id":1031724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031690#post1031690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Dauntain are so damn cool (from an ST perspective, I doubt PCs would agree) now! \ud83d\ude03</div> </div> </div> </div>*cackle* Many dials were broken in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:58:09-08:00","id":1031749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031722#post1031722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Banality kills magic. That's kind of the point. Autumn People have certain abilities derived from Banality, but it's not the same as having Banal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I depends on your point of view.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned Dountain powers work(ed) as Magic, therefore they were mahic. <br /> <br /> Also Technocracy is considered to be Banal and has Magic. Ergo, Banality doesn't kill magic. It changes magic. <br /> <br /> What Banality kills is anything, that comes from the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Specifically. Sometimes it hunts, sometimes haunts, sometime it taints. Dauntain is a testament of that. <br /> <br /> Banality is magic. <br /> <br /> Well, was, considering the changes.<br /> <br /> Ask Mages, they will tell the same thing. Well, at least some of them. <br /> <br /> Except for Technocrats, they will tell you, that there is no magic and therefore there can't be &quot;Banality/Reason&quot; magic. <br /> <br /> As far as they're concerned, where reason, education and commons sense goes, Reality Warpers and other invaders loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-14-2017, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:05:15-08:00","id":1031755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031749#post1031749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I depends on your point of view.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned Dountain powers work(ed) as Magic, therefore they were mahic.<br /> <br /> Also Technocracy is considered to be Banal and has Magic. Ergo, Banality doesn't kill magic. It changes magic.<br /> <br /> What Banality kills is anything, that comes from the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Specifically. Sometimes it hunts, sometimes haunts, sometime it taints. Dauntain is a testament of that.<br /> <br /> Banality is magic.<br /> <br /> Well, was, considering the changes.<br /> <br /> Ask Mages, they will tell the same thing. Well, at least some of them.<br /> <br /> Except for Technocrats, they will tell you, that there is no magic and therefore there can't be &quot;Banality/Reason&quot; magic.<br /> <br /> As far as they're concerned, where reason, education and commons sense goes, Reality Warpers and other invaders loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banality destroys magic. It eats away at it gradually, over time. It backlashes violently when magic occurs. If you're citing Mage as source material, you're forgetting that there's a difference between &quot;coincidental&quot; and &quot;vulgar&quot; magic. Coincidental is the kind of thing that doesn't offend reality, what people believe can happen, or how people believe it /could/ happen. Reality has an ugly tendency to hurt mages who flash their rotes too loudly. <br /> <br /> That's Banality, trying to kill the magic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:15:10-08:00","id":1031763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031749#post1031749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I depends on your point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose this isn't terribly helpful, but I find it amusing. You are arguing with one of the writers about <i>how</i> the setting works.<br /> <br /> All in all, reading this thread has been enlightening. Looking forward to getting my copy of C20 eventually.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:22:04-08:00","id":1031767,"title":"","content":"@Maggie C<br /> Someone of us had seen glimpses of C20 and it wasn't me. <br /> <br /> I don't see any point in arguing, if you base your opinion on a source I have no familiarity, which revises the whole setting, BTW.<br /> <br /> Blind people and elephant much. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:39:57-08:00","id":1031780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031767#post1031767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Maggie C<br /> Someone of us had seen glimpses of C20 and it wasn't me.<br /> <br /> I don't see any point in arguing, if you base your opinion on a source I have no familiarity, which revises the whole setting, BTW.<br /> <br /> Blind people and elephant much. )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not really sure what you're getting at here. I am aware it revises the setting. Not sure what the parable has to do with it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:44:10-08:00","id":1031785,"title":"","content":"Banality, it's definition and functionality changed from book to book, sometimes from chapter to chapter, thoughout the Changeling books line.<br /> <br /> I'm drawing my conclusions from the books I've read. Autumn People was the biggest give away, that Banality was magical in it's nature. <br /> <br /> If it's retconned, the definition of Banality will probably change, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-14-2017, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:06:09-08:00","id":1031804,"title":"","content":"Autumn People was a first edition book, and was retconned already at least a little with Changeling 2nd Edition. <br /> <br /> While I enjoyed the book, I felt it tried to make Banality do something it wasn't meant to do, something that jarred the notion of what made a changeling a changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":