udden doublepost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:27:24-08:00","id":1031875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031821#post1031821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Agendas were stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'll be pleased then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T19:07:28-08:00","id":1031916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031821#post1031821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Agendas were stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cry Woof (that allowed Autumn People to summon nexus crawlers) specifically is quite terrible, both because nexus crawlers are of the Wyrm rather than the Weaver (this was before it became a major antagonist with stasis vectors, granted), but because one of either is a likely TPK for any given motley not 300% dedicated to kicking ass (full of trolls, numuz'ho, canotilli, solomonds and gloams, maybe some visiting hsien with high Dao and Neidan as well), and also <i>some less experienced Garou packs</i>. This is even more true in the 20th anniversary editions, when such spirits can have Essence capacities clocking in at 80 or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:38:05-08:00","id":1031998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1031916#post1031916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cry Woof (that allowed Autumn People to summon nexus crawlers) specifically is quite terrible, both because nexus crawlers are of the Wyrm rather than the Weaver (this was before it became a major antagonist with stasis vectors, granted), but because one of either is a likely TPK for any given motley not 300% dedicated to kicking ass (full of trolls, numuz'ho, canotilli, solomonds and gloams, maybe some visiting hsien with high Dao and Neidan as well), and also <i>some less experienced Garou packs</i>. This is even more true in the 20th anniversary editions, when such spirits can have Essence capacities clocking in at 80 or more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no. They can't do that anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T00:28:27-08:00","id":1032030,"title":"","content":"BTW, how new Changelings handle things, like characters being excited and inspired by science, reason and rationality, but considering knights, magic and fairy tales to be quite boring... unimagintive and even <i>lazy</i>.<br /> <br /> Could someome be both creative/imaginative and think, that changeling society is too full of <i>clich\u00e9s</i>?<br /> <br /> Could an awakened kithain see the chimeric reality as patterns of math, interactions of particles and waves and complex webs of mystery, waiting to be unwoven?<br /> <br /> Or kithain are pretty much stuck in their 'fantasy' paradigms, like flies in amber?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-15-2017, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T01:18:22-08:00","id":1032039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032030#post1032030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, how new Changelings handle things, like characters being excited and inspired by science, reason and rationality, but considering knights, magic and fairy tales to be quite boring... unimagintive and even <i>lazy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valid possibilities for characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could someome be both creative/imaginative and think, that changeling society is too full of <i>clich\u00e9s</i>? </div> </div> </div>Yes. See also: how commoners tend to view sidhe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could an awakened kithain see the chimeric reality as patterns of math, interactions of particles and waves and complex webs of mystery, waiting to be unwoven? </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. The Dreaming shifts in accordance with the ambient dreams of the humans around it. I imagine it might be something similar to this around technical colleges like MIT or CalTech.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or kithain are pretty much stuck in their 'fantasy' paradigms, like flies in amber? </div> </div> </div>Some are. Some aren't. Changelings are still people, and like people, are unique in their personality, mentality and quirks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T01:28:19-08:00","id":1032042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032030#post1032030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, how new Changelings handle things, like characters being excited and inspired by science, reason and rationality, but considering knights, magic and fairy tales to be quite boring... unimagintive and even <i>lazy</i>.<br /> <br /> Could someome be both creative/imaginative and think, that changeling society is too full of <i>clich\u00e9s</i>?<br /> <br /> Could an awakened kithain see the chimeric reality as patterns of math, interactions of particles and waves and complex webs of mystery, waiting to be unwoven?<br /> <br /> Or kithain are pretty much stuck in their 'fantasy' paradigms, like flies in amber?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing they could interpret what they see that way, although Changeling never went into the specific subjectivity of the Dreaming a la videres. I mean, yes, it's subjective, or rather it's responsive to the people passing through it, but I'm not sure it's the same as the Umbra where three mages with different paradigms and Essences could see slightly different things. I always assumed there was a kind of objective reality to it, which is the paradigm of myth and dream, or the collective unconscious writ large. Locally, this adapts to dreamers, but three changelings standing next to each other probably all see the same thing even if that thing is shaped by all three of them. If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> In which case, the science-loving fae might see balloons and bunny rabbits but understand them as wasted dreaming energy taking a form suggested by the observer, in much the same way heat is wasted energy in other reactions and processes, and in the same way waves and particles only become one or the other when observed. He might understand will-o'-wisps in terms of refraction and reflection, and Glamour in terms of the physics of consciousness. There's loads of fun there for a keen player. But, in essence, he's still seeing the same thing as the other characters--it's just a matter of how he interprets what he sees.<br /> <br /> Now, C20 may introduce something like videres for the Dreaming (or I may just have missed it), but I suspect this would be an extra layer of complication the game shies away from, just because players already sometimes struggle with the duality of real/chimerical as it is, without making everyone's version of chimerical reality also unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T08:06:07-08:00","id":1032133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032042#post1032042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing they could interpret what they see that way, although Changeling never went into the specific subjectivity of the Dreaming a la videres. I mean, yes, it's subjective, or rather it's responsive to the people passing through it, but I'm not sure it's the same as the Umbra where three mages with different paradigms and Essences could see slightly different things. I always assumed there was a kind of objective reality to it, which is the paradigm of myth and dream, or the collective unconscious writ large. Locally, this adapts to dreamers, but three changelings standing next to each other probably all see the same thing even if that thing is shaped by all three of them. If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> In which case, the science-loving fae might see balloons and bunny rabbits but understand them as wasted dreaming energy taking a form suggested by the observer, in much the same way heat is wasted energy in other reactions and processes, and in the same way waves and particles only become one or the other when observed. He might understand will-o'-wisps in terms of refraction and reflection, and Glamour in terms of the physics of consciousness. There's loads of fun there for a keen player. But, in essence, he's still seeing the same thing as the other characters--it's just a matter of how he interprets what he sees.<br /> <br /> Now, C20 may introduce something like videres for the Dreaming (or I may just have missed it), but I suspect this would be an extra layer of complication the game shies away from, just because players already sometimes struggle with the duality of real/chimerical as it is, without making everyone's version of chimerical reality also unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also because it isn't Mage, the only game that really puts that much subjectivity into anything. A mage of some belief or another might believe that all spiritual dimensions they see are the realm of the dead, but Werewolf, Wraith, and Changeling can generally agree that their respective stomping grounds are very, very different and distinct, with Changeling getting the Dreaming pretty much all to itself and distinguishing it from spirit locales by the implications of the Spirit Link Art. KotE throws its lot in here too, putting all manner of different realms in distinctly different places such that it'd be very difficult for any group of observers to mistake one for the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:05:11-08:00","id":1032190,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Changeling and Mage share the idea that human belief determines reality. How the two games implement it is pretty different. In Mage, you can have two people view the same thing and potentially see something wildly different based on their respective paradigms.<br /> <br /> In Changeling, two changelings or enchanted humans will always see the same dream realm or patch of chimeric reality as the same thing. The piece of the Dreaming they're both viewing will change over time as the local legends change though.<br /> <br /> Something I've always thought was neat about the Dreaming is how certain archetypes keep appearing pretty much regardless of the dreams that shape the local area. As an example, dragons seem to be native to just about everywhere in the Dreaming. Even areas reflecting high tech dreams still have techo-dragons with laser wings. It's almost as though they've achieved a level of permanence in the Dreaming. How long does a dream have to endure to become a permanent fixture in the ever changing Glamour? Also, how ancient were the beings that first dreamed them into existence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T15:37:32-08:00","id":1032348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032190#post1032190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've always thought was neat about the Dreaming is how certain archetypes keep appearing pretty much regardless of the dreams that shape the local area. As an example, dragons seem to be native to just about everywhere in the Dreaming. Even areas reflecting high tech dreams still have techo-dragons with laser wings. It's almost as though they've achieved a level of permanence in the Dreaming. How long does a dream have to endure to become a permanent fixture in the ever changing Glamour? Also, how ancient were the beings that first dreamed them into existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>And is it the same dragon that was always there, adjusting to the shifting consensus of dreams of the neighbourhood, or did that dragon get replaced by a new dragon more in alignment with the new ambience dictated by the saturation of techno-Dreamers? Stuff fae philosophers argue about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:34:43-08:00","id":1032371,"title":"","content":"Im curious about the Chimera. since they are dream's and nightmares...is it possible for one to go around killing people a la &quot;The Corinthian&quot; from Sandman?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:40:41-08:00","id":1032379,"title":"","content":"If it is powerful enough, it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:47:02-08:00","id":1032381,"title":"","content":"Under certain circumstances. If they have the Wyrd Rede, for instance, they can affect the Autumn World the same as the Dreaming. Their chimerical damage can become bashing or lethal damage. Think more like Freddy Kreuger as a nightmare chimera, or the ghosts in Supernatural who suddenly manifest and throw people across the room. It's not necessarily exactly like that, but it's a good visual along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:04:56-08:00","id":1032392,"title":"","content":"By the way, chimeras without Wyrd and Enchantment redes, could they interact with inanimate object of Autumn World? Open and close doors, steal things?<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, I wrote chimera (very noncanonl, teeheee) once, centered around three Redes: <i>Wyrd</i>, <i>Enchntment</i> and <i>Archtype</i>. <a href=\"http://lunargods.blogspot.com/2016/01/tobby.html\" target=\"_blank\">Mostly, as a joke</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:11:14-08:00","id":1032394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032392#post1032392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, chimeras without Wyrd and Enchantment redes, could they interact with inanimate object of Autumn World? Open and close doors, steal things?<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, I wrote chimera (very noncanonl, teeheee) once, centered around three Redes: <i>Wyrd</i>, <i>Enchntment</i> and <i>Archtype</i>. <a href=\"http://lunargods.blogspot.com/2016/01/tobby.html\" target=\"_blank\">Mostly, as a joke</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, that's a difficult question to answer. I don't want to say no, because there are always, always exceptions, but I don't want to say yes either, because it's not strictly true. I'll just put it this way: it depends on the nature of the chimera, what dreams they spring from, what dreams they're meant to embody, and how they sustain themselves. It's my <i>personal</i> view that the Dream should trump mechanical Redes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T20:24:18-08:00","id":1032455,"title":"","content":"I was talking with some friends about changeling and how do they feed on glamour by Inspiring people.....<br /> <br /> Could we say that Lovecraft is what happend when an Unseelie member is bored and meets a very creative writter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T22:02:41-08:00","id":1032479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032455#post1032455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking with some friends about changeling and how do they feed on glamour by Inspiring people.....<br /> <br /> Could we say that Lovecraft is what happend when an Unseelie member is bored and meets a very creative writter?</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that because the changeling was bored, he inspired HP to pad his word count even more excessively than the concerns of being paid by the word would have padded them alone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T22:10:06-08:00","id":1032481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032479#post1032479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're saying that because the changeling was bored, he inspired HP to pad his word count even more excessively than the concerns of being paid by the word would have padded them alone?</div> </div> </div> </div>im saying, i cant stop imagining a changeling putting extra spicey nightmares on lovecraft so he could get more &quot;clear&quot; visions of the eldtrich horrors","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T23:01:57-08:00","id":1032498,"title":"","content":"If that's how it goes in your version of the world, that's how it goes. <br /> <br /> Unseelie, though, doesn't mean &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;malicious&quot; by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T23:08:27-08:00","id":1032503,"title":"","content":"I don't know why it would have to be a bored Unseelie. Inspiring horror writers to scare people in new and terrifying ways seems like a pretty good way to gather Glamour for an Unseelie who doesn't want to ravage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T23:41:14-08:00","id":1032512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032503#post1032503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why it would have to be a bored Unseelie. Inspiring horror writers to scare people in new and terrifying ways seems like a pretty good way to gather Glamour for an Unseelie who doesn't want to ravage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you wanted to stick with the evil, malicious torture schtick, Lovecraft suffered sleep paralysis and parasomnia. There are creatures of the Dreaming that could either take advantage of this, or or cause them as a side effect, like some Thallain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T04:32:02-08:00","id":1032588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032481#post1032481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> im saying, i cant stop imagining a changeling putting extra spicey nightmares on lovecraft so he could get more &quot;clear&quot; visions of the eldtrich horrors</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, you're misunderstanding the nature of Lovecraftian Horror. <br /> <br /> It's not about scary monsters, zombies, fish people and living instentines aliens. <br /> <br /> Lovecraftian Horror is horror of unknown and unknowable. The realization of one's absolute cosmic insignificance. &quot;Gods&quot; exist and they aren't humanlike nor loving. By humanity's standards, they're evil and to have a glimpse of them and their favor you have to commit inhuman atrocities and turn into monster. Being closer to them means loosing last shreds of humanity and sanity, loosing yourself into creeping madness. <br /> <br /> And gods themselves do not care. <br /> <br /> Not, that I find it particularly scary.<br /> <br /> But the point is, that showing nightmares and visions of nightmarish dreaming wouldn't affect Lovecraft's way of writing. <br /> <br /> Not more or less, than any other kind of Reverie. <br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but I have a feeling, that Lovecraft's fiction is not a notes of scared boy, who seen the horror and wanted to share his fears. I think it's deliberate philosophical critique of society and one Unseelie changeling might've been not create a tide. <br /> <br /> Dunno, I'd suggest you to read Lovecraft himself (except for his racist remarks), what he thinks of his works and why he did wrote them, before making decision. <br /> <br /> Maybe, Lovecraft inspired some bored Unseelie Sluagh. <br /> Or maybe, in World of Darkness he was healed by a wandering healer and wrote something different, and there is no Mythos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-16-2017, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:54:58-08:00","id":1032804,"title":"","content":"Ok, i got more questions.<br /> <br /> One: Can a changeling &quot;multi task&quot; in both banal reality and chimerical reality? Example: Todd's wife has seen him very busy working his taxes lately, doing all the accounting in his house... but could he actually be preparing cantrips from the Chimerical reality point of view?.. or could two seniors be on a park, playing chess while in the chimerical reality they are practicing fencing? or must one reflect on the other?<br /> <br /> Second: how does a changeling joins a House? can any changeling join a House?<br /> <br /> Third: When a changeling stops being a commoner and joins nobility? i mean is there a merit or a background that allows the PC's be nobility ?<br /> <br /> Fourth: Lets say that Todd's wife dies on a car crash. she doesn't turn into a Wraith. His depression is so much that he decided to make a Chimera based off her and the memories he has of her....is this possible? to make chimera's of our loved ones? and if so, how badly seen would be for the courts/houses ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-16-2017, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:16:40-08:00","id":1032871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032804#post1032804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One: Can a changeling &quot;multi task&quot; in both banal reality and chimerical reality? Example: Todd's wife has seen him very busy working his taxes lately, doing all the accounting in his house... but could he actually be preparing cantrips from the Chimerical reality point of view?.. or could two seniors be on a park, playing chess while in the chimerical reality they are practicing fencing? or must one reflect on the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mists only cloud the minds of unenchanted onlookers. It doesn't give changelings a supernatural ability to do two completely different tasks at once (that's what cantrips are for \ud83d\ude09 ). If a changeling is doing his taxes, that's what he's doing. That being said, a changeling who specializes in financial matters could totally use a creative tax work as a bunk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second: how does a changeling joins a House? can any changeling join a House? </div> </div> </div>A changeling joins a house either by being recognized as having membership in the house that transcends his current lifetime or by impressing leaders within the house and being asked to join. Theoretically, any kith could potentially join any house. In practice though, certain houses are more accepting of certain kiths than others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third: When a changeling stops being a commoner and joins nobility? i mean is there a merit or a background that allows the PC's be nobility ? </div> </div> </div>The Title background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:34:36-08:00","id":1032882,"title":"","content":"This one got added after my response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032804#post1032804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth: Lets say that Todd's wife dies on a car crash. she doesn't turn into a Wraith. His depression is so much that he decided to make a Chimera based off her and the memories he has of her....is this possible? to make chimera's of our loved ones? and if so, how badly seen would be for the courts/houses ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. It's certainly not something that's normally done, but it certainly seems possible to do. The resulting chimera won't be the actual person, just an imperfect copy. Even the Art of Spring isn't capable of true resurrection.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I could see several plausible consequences. Because of his inability to let go and accept the changes that are part and parcel with life and instead preferring stasis, he might be inviting a Banality trigger. The way others react to him would vary from individual to individual. His own reaction might change as he realizes the chimera isn't actually his dead wife. Over time, he might grow to resent his creation, or he might learn to accept it as a new, unique chimerical individual. In any case, I could see lots of good fodder for a chronicle there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:58:57-08:00","id":1032895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032882#post1032882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one got added after my response.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Good question. It's certainly not something that's normally done, but it certainly seems possible to do. The resulting chimera won't be the actual person, just an imperfect copy. Even the Art of Spring isn't capable of true resurrection.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I could see several plausible consequences. Because of his inability to let go and accept the changes that are part and parcel with life and instead preferring stasis, he might be inviting a Banality trigger. The way others react to him would vary from individual to individual. His own reaction might change as he realizes the chimera isn't actually his dead wife. Over time, he might grow to resent his creation, or he might learn to accept it as a new, unique chimerical individual. In any case, I could see lots of good fodder for a chronicle there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah. It isn't... exactly Pygmalion here, and chimera creation in the sense that you mean isn't completely understood \u2014 some chimera just come to life on their own, while others that might have been created at the same time remain mindless. Some chimera are very good at faking the appearance of self-awareness, but they're just cleverly programmed (in the sense of forged chimera especially). Some attain sentience just as their creator intended, and others were never meant to be sentient, but wake up one day with a sense of self-identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:37:20-08:00","id":1032923,"title":"","content":"Art of Spring ? Jeez... I eager for the release of C20.<br /> <br /> I have a question about something I have trouble to understand in the rulebook. It's about Enchantment and the difficulty of cantrips on mortals. I've seen at several place in the book that Enchanting a mortal helps a Changeling to cast cantrip on him because he had already circumvent his Banality. But nowhere in the Enchantment or Arts rules I've seen something close to that statement.<br /> Is it that the Banality of the mortal is dropping when I enchant him or am I missing something? The first possibility makes sense but I don't remember seeing anything about a drop of the Banality rate in the rule on Enchantment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:09:02-08:00","id":1032940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032882#post1032882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one got added after my response.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Good question. It's certainly not something that's normally done, but it certainly seems possible to do. The resulting chimera won't be the actual person, just an imperfect copy. Even the Art of Spring isn't capable of true resurrection.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I could see several plausible consequences. Because of his inability to let go and accept the changes that are part and parcel with life and instead preferring stasis, he might be inviting a Banality trigger. The way others react to him would vary from individual to individual. His own reaction might change as he realizes the chimera isn't actually his dead wife. Over time, he might grow to resent his creation, or he might learn to accept it as a new, unique chimerical individual. In any case, I could see lots of good fodder for a chronicle there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So. Promethean the Dreamed? Hahah!!....yeah..sorry had to...<br /> <br /> Can a chimera be an actual firearm?. i tend to notice that Changeling and Medieval go hand in hand.. so thats why i wonder how do changelings feel about firearms and so on, for both chimerical creation to even pull a bloody boomstick against a troll with an ax<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:35:16-08:00","id":1032950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032940#post1032940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a chimera be an actual firearm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Of sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:41:28-08:00","id":1032960,"title":"","content":"Nockers LOVE firearms! <br /> <br /> I don't think, much more else can be said. <br /> <br /> Also, considering, that chimera and fae tend to be ideals (in Plato's sense) the biggest danger might be that such chimera will be too much like a person it replaces. A perfect replice. Just enough good traits and just enough bed ones. Lotus Eater Machine of sorts. <br /> <br /> For example I can imagine such chimera assuming skills and Redes to fullfil that role so well, that it will be the only person, Changeling cares about. To the point it'll start feeding from Changeling's memories and Glamour to feed it's &quot;realness&quot;. <br /> <br /> Also good thing for self-perpetuating Bedlam.<br /> <br /> It might be a good antagonist, but also interesting character background that will dominate player character's arc.<br /> <br /> O, damn, I remembered it was a thing in Shining Host?.. But it was a stranger lover. All ideas are old. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, how realistic can be playing a chimera in C20? <br /> <br /> Can't recall, whether stretch goal for Chimera expansion was taken or not...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-16-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:16:42-08:00","id":1032973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032960#post1032960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how realistic can be playing a chimera in C20? <br /> <br /> Can't recall, whether stretch goal for Chimera expansion was taken or not...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no rules for playing chimera as PCs. That being said, Bygone Beastiary has rules that could be adapted for it.<br /> <br /> Also, the stretch goal for expanded info on chimera wasn't met.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:27:24-08:00","id":1032981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032960#post1032960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nockers LOVE firearms!<br /> <br /> I don't think, much more else can be said.<br /> <br /> Also, considering, that chimera and fae tend to be ideals (in Plato's sense) the biggest danger might be that such chimera will be too much like a person it replaces. A perfect replice. Just enough good traits and just enough bed ones. Lotus Eater Machine of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimera spring from dreams, either the ambient dreams of an area that reflects that area in some way, or direct dreams. They can be created by changelings. They can be created by other chimera. They're not really Platonic ideals, since they can be abstracts, absurdities, or parallels. They're not Real Forms. A chimera birthed from the grief a person losing their partner will likely be touched by the emotions and thoughts that gave it substance, and might not be harmless. It could feed on the person's darker emotions, drive them deeper into it. It might not even be birthed from the person's desire to see their partner again, but an extant chimera using Redes like Shapeshift and Befuddle to mimic the dead partner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how realistic can be playing a chimera in C20?<br /> <br /> Can't recall, whether stretch goal for Chimera expansion was taken or not... </div> </div> </div>I don't recall it as a stretch goal, but chimera creation and various kinds of chimera are detailed in the C20 core book. I probably wouldn't allow a player to create one, since they're not really meant to be player character options, IMO, but Storyteller tools. I suppose you could use the rules to play one, but I'm not sure how broad the game would be in scope. Chimera are pretty limited to just the Dreaming, and often to their particular area of the Dreaming, without certain Redes that tend to be rare (and expensive in point-buy cost).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:33:05-08:00","id":1032984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032981#post1032981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chimera spring from dreams, either the ambient dreams of an area that reflects that area in some way, or direct dreams. They can be created by changelings. They can be created by other chimera. They're not really Platonic ideals, since they can be abstracts, absurdities, or parallels. They're not Real Forms. A chimera birthed from the grief a person losing their partner will likely be touched by the emotions and thoughts that gave it substance, and might not be harmless. It could feed on the person's darker emotions, drive them deeper into it. It might not even be birthed from the person's desire to see their partner again, but an extant chimera using Redes like Shapeshift and Befuddle to mimic the dead partner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't recall it as a stretch goal, but chimera creation and various kinds of chimera are detailed in the C20 core book. I probably wouldn't allow a player to create one, since they're not really meant to be player character options, IMO, but Storyteller tools. I suppose you could use the rules to play one, but I'm not sure how broad the game would be in scope. Chimera are pretty limited to just the Dreaming, and often to their particular area of the Dreaming, without certain Redes that tend to be rare (and expensive in point-buy cost).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just how much glamour and effort do a changeling has to spend to create a chimera?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:38:05-08:00","id":1032990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032984#post1032984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how much glamour and effort do a changeling has to spend to create a chimera?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be telling. And I can't do that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:56:03-08:00","id":1033002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032990#post1032990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would be telling. And I can't do that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay,okay. How about. Can new changeling kiths be born in this modern age? Say, an kith based on urban myths like slender man or bloody Mary, or a techo-kith that embodies technology as opposed to the knockers who use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:58:24-08:00","id":1033003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033002#post1033002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay,okay. How about. Can new changeling kiths be born in this modern age? Say, an kith based on urban myths like slender man or bloody Mary, or a techo-kith that embodies technology as opposed to the knockers who use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mwahahaha, there's a thing I wrote in C20 to specifically answer that question \ud83d\ude08","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"rea