tyle=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3785_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3785\" data-vbnamecard=\"3785\">Luka C</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a> . Y'all know hwat a changeling fan wants :&gt;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone who worked on the book is a Changeling fan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T20:11:16-08:00","id":1033109,"title":"","content":"I know its impossible but..any chances to get a shout out in the book? like a side character in one of the short character's stories or something like that?. Its a bloody dream of mine to be in a rpg book even if its as a casual mention xD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:06:53-08:00","id":1033194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033109#post1033109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know its impossible but..any chances to get a shout out in the book? like a side character in one of the short character's stories or something like that?. Its a bloody dream of mine to be in a rpg book even if its as a casual mention xD</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, the C20 text has been locked down for quite awhile now.<br /> <br /> Watch for future Kickstarters though. There's usually a reward level to get your character in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:21:54-08:00","id":1033224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032981#post1032981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chimera spring from dreams, either the ambient dreams of an area that reflects that area in some way, or direct dreams. They can be created by changelings. They can be created by other chimera. They're not really Platonic ideals, since they can be abstracts, absurdities, or parallels. They're not Real Forms. A chimera birthed from the grief a person losing their partner will likely be touched by the emotions and thoughts that gave it substance, and might not be harmless. It could feed on the person's darker emotions, drive them deeper into it. It might not even be birthed from the person's desire to see their partner again, but an extant chimera using Redes like Shapeshift and Befuddle to mimic the dead partner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't recall it as a stretch goal, but chimera creation and various kinds of chimera are detailed in the C20 core book. I probably wouldn't allow a player to create one, since they're not really meant to be player character options, IMO, but Storyteller tools. I suppose you could use the rules to play one, but I'm not sure how broad the game would be in scope. Chimera are pretty limited to just the Dreaming, and often to their particular area of the Dreaming, without certain Redes that tend to be rare (and expensive in point-buy cost).</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, chimera can be quite different. There's Dreamed ones, that is part of changeling's background or if they're powerful enough, a companions. There are golems, etc. Also, if you're not taking special traits, Adhene pretty much limited in their access to Autmn World too, as they have no bodies - therefore chimera-like. <br /> <br /> It doesn't seem all that implausible. Just not for chronicles with very specific premise, focused on banality and humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T03:57:32-08:00","id":1033256,"title":"","content":"Playing a chimera as a character and having a chimera as parts of a character's origin story or panoply are two different things. Which did you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:17:10-08:00","id":1033300,"title":"","content":"is it possible to lower the rating of permanent banality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:24:08-08:00","id":1033306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033300#post1033300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it possible to lower the rating of permanent banality?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, but it ain't easy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:11:19-08:00","id":1033338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033306#post1033306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yep, but it ain't easy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, i think i probably know the answer to that one, but just to be sure,. technology isn't always banal anymore right? i can get glamour from a little kid playing her boxjust as easy as the same kid drawing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:47:51-08:00","id":1033357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033338#post1033338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, i think i probably know the answer to that one, but just to be sure,. technology isn't always banal anymore right? i can get glamour from a little kid playing her boxjust as easy as the same kid drawing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Science and technology are not inherently banal, no. It's all about how they're used and the practitioners' approach to them. Someone building a new raspberry pi implementation is just as glamourous as someone composing a sonnet. Both are potential sources of Glamour, but if they're just mindlessly following a rote method, then they can both be banal too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:11:12-08:00","id":1033370,"title":"","content":"So...a man like Neil Degrass Tyson who is incredibly creative is banal. mainly because in his world view the universe has an order and meaning.<br /> <br /> While someone like Dali would be a waterfall of glamour since his world is completely upside down and he doesnt look for a logic but to perform &quot;The Art&quot;<br /> <br /> just making sure to differenciate between two kinds of creativity, the glamour and banal one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:12:39-08:00","id":1033371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033370#post1033370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...a man like Neil Degrass Tyson who is incredibly creative is banal. mainly because in his world view the universe has an order and meaning.<br /> <br /> While someone like Dali would be a waterfall of glamour since his world is completely upside down and he doesnt look for a logic but to perform &quot;The Art&quot;<br /> <br /> just making sure to differenciate between two kinds of creativity, the glamour and banal one</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's..... not what I said at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:13:16-08:00","id":1033372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1029889#post1029889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgot this one:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the cosmology of Changeling: The Dreaming, there are two major worlds the Kithain deal with \u2014 Earth and the Dreaming. Certain changeling scholars have heard of various other realms that their prodigal cousins interact with, but they tend to view those realms as subsets within one of these two worlds.<br /> <br /> Earth is pretty much the same as the real word, only a little darker, colder, and more hopeless. On the other side of the Mists, the Dreaming is comprised of a nearly infinite number of realms and kingdoms. Some of these realms are merely a passing flight of fancy lasting no more than a single night. Others are permanent fixtures upon the dreamscape that predate the Kithain and their progenitors, the Tuatha de Dannan. The deeper one travels into the Dreaming and farther away one gets from the Banality of Earth, the more fantastic and closer to the old myths the realms of the Dreaming become. At the center of the Dreaming stands Arcadia, the pillar that supports the entirety of the Dreaming and the realm the Kithain claim as their homeland. The gates to Arcadia are lost, obscured by the Mists. None outside Arcadia may enter lest they poison it by their taint of Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any fae on earth Who didnt used the changeling way butbmanagedbto survive the wave not banality big the last centuries? Or just the sidhe are 100% Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:18:46-08:00","id":1033374,"title":"","content":"Lost Ones technically survived without undergoing the Changeling Way, but I don't think they're an example anyone wants to follow.<br /> <br /> The Innanimae didn't got the Changeling Way route either, but their Husks provide them with a similar level of protection.<br /> <br /> All that being said, the Arcadian sidhe on Earth aren't 100% fae either. They had to become changelings to survive, they just didn't adopt the Changeling Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:23:28-08:00","id":1033376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033374#post1033374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost Ones technically survived without undergoing the Changeling Way, but I don't think they're an example anyone wants to follow.<br /> <br /> The Innanimae didn't got the Changeling Way route either, but their Husks provide them with a similar level of protection.<br /> <br /> All that being said, the Arcadian sidhe on Earth aren't 100% fae either. They had to become changelings to survive, they just didn't adopt the Changeling Way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering Mister Cantrell. Sorry for my typing mistakes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:27:03-08:00","id":1033380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033370#post1033370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just making sure to differenciate between two kinds of creativity, the glamour and banal one</div> </div> </div> </div>There shouldn't be a banal form of creativity.<br /> <br /> If something is creative, it has the potential for Glamour. Just how much depends on what we're talking about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:33:06-08:00","id":1033383,"title":"","content":"There's a level to Banality that's entirely personal. I would have no problem doing paper stock inventory at school, for instance, because I'm a paper nerd. I love the feel of different weights and finishes, textures and colors. I can look at every ream and see the possibilities in the grains, the art and purposes it might be used for. <br /> <br /> It's a mind numbing job to someone else, who just sees it as counting up reams of paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":3785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","user":"Luka C","date":". 01-17-2017, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:49:41-08:00","id":1033389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033383#post1033383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a level to Banality that's entirely personal. I would have no problem doing paper stock inventory at school, for instance, because I'm a paper nerd. I love the feel of different weights and finishes, textures and colors. I can look at every ream and see the possibilities in the grains, the art and purposes it might be used for.<br /> <br /> It's a mind numbing job to someone else, who just sees it as counting up reams of paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooooh, we're talking about this piece! That's something I can't wait to get out there and see everyone's reactions! I'm so happy with how it turned out and how the other thing ties into it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T09:16:49-08:00","id":1033398,"title":"","content":"by the way, just wondering....is there any homages to the late Goblin King David Bowie on the book? can you confirm, deny or give a hint?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T09:51:35-08:00","id":1033412,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure a couple of small Labyrinth references survived through to the final text.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> But of course, nothing is set in stone until the book is in print.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:18:18-08:00","id":1033430,"title":"","content":"Pop culture referencea don't always make it through the development process. In the grand scheme of things, it's like trying to get a Balrog past Gandalf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:07:30-08:00","id":1033476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033370#post1033370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...a man like Neil Degrass Tyson who is incredibly creative is banal. mainly because in his world view the universe has an order and meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that Neil Degrass Tyson is the polar opposite of Banality. He's probably the best example I could conjure of science as a Glamour font. Using it to illuminate and inspire and generate wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:28:06-08:00","id":1033488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033476#post1033476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that Neil Degrass Tyson is the polar opposite of Banality. He's probably the best example I could conjure of science as a Glamour font. Using it to illuminate and inspire and generate wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>i thought Scientific creativity (explaining and decoding the world) would be banal inducing...So..anything that can inspire and move generations (pure Dynamism) would be Glamour, while the thought patterns/ideas that relate to &quot;Stop&quot; or Statism would be Banality?<br /> <br /> it makes me think of a comic i read <a href=\"http://zenpencils.com/comic/kevinsmith/\" target=\"_blank\">http://zenpencils.com/comic/kevinsmith/</a> &quot;Discourage an artist, and you get absolutely nothing in return, ever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:30:54-08:00","id":1033493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033488#post1033488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i thought Scientific creativity (explaining and decoding the world) would be banal inducing...So..anything that can inspire and move generations (pure Dynamism) would be Glamour, while the thought patterns/ideas that relate to &quot;Stop&quot; or Statism would be Banality?<br /> <br /> it makes me think of a comic i read <a href=\"http://zenpencils.com/comic/kevinsmith/\" target=\"_blank\">http://zenpencils.com/comic/kevinsmith/</a> &quot;Discourage an artist, and you get absolutely nothing in return, ever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Having explanations for things isn't banality. Understanding how things work isn't Banality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:33:17-08:00","id":1033497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033476#post1033476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that Neil Degrass Tyson is the polar opposite of Banality. He's probably the best example I could conjure of science as a Glamour font. Using it to illuminate and inspire and generate wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would certainly agree. He's fantastic at inspiring people, getting them out of their rut, and questioning all sorts of unexamined assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T11:38:21-08:00","id":1033502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033497#post1033497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would certainly agree. He's fantastic at inspiring people, getting them out of their rut, and questioning all sorts of unexamined assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Michio Kaku also. He enjoys explaining ways sci fi technology might come around. Mythbusters. How Things Work. Penn &amp; Teller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:02:09-08:00","id":1033524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033488#post1033488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i thought Scientific creativity (explaining and decoding the world) would be banal inducing...So..anything that can inspire and move generations (pure Dynamism) would be Glamour, while the thought patterns/ideas that relate to &quot;Stop&quot; or Statism would be Banality?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's talk science and Glamour real quick \u2014 at it's core science is a method for exploring the unknown. It works by questioning dogma and forcing those who follow it to constantly reexamine long held beliefs. In practice, nearly every question it answers raises many more. Creativity is an essential bedrock of science because each new question requires researchers and theorists to come up with whole new avenues of inquiry.<br /> <br /> The world only feels quantified because we're surrounded by technological marvels undreamed of only a generation or two ago. Once you look past that, you see that the biggest take away from the research that went into creating that technology is how little we truly understand about the universe and its workings. It's wondrous, and almost no one who takes the time to really look into it can come away without an unquenchable curiosity about what we as a species will learn next.<br /> <br /> This sense of wonder and curiosity along with our culture is unique among humanity. It's the fire that the Tuatha de Danaan stoked and made theirs to give them and us ascendancy over the Fomorian Dream. In that sense, science, when approached with wonder and curiosity, is part and parcel of Glamour.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, too many people are satisfied with the incomplete answers. They settle for mediocrity, content to wallow in the rut they've carved out for themselves. That's the heart of Banality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-17-2017, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:02:52-08:00","id":1033525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1033502#post1033502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michio Kaku also. He enjoys explaining ways sci fi technology might come around. Mythbusters. How Things Work. Penn &amp; Teller.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:32:11-08:00","id":1033550,"title":"","content":"ok So...if the science or work you do can inspire you or others to achive new things. either be science, art, philosophy etc.. is glamour<br /> <br /> But, if deprives inspiration, its stagnated and doenst allow a margin to be creative. its Banal... hurmm...<br /> now i cant stop thinking of Office Space as a Changeling Movie...or Fight Club for that matter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:44:59-08:00","id":1033564,"title":"","content":"Now you're getting it. And just to be clear, Glamour isn't relegated to solely &quot;positive&quot; emotions. Love and hatred, joy and sorrow, laughter and fear \u2014 what ever kicks a person out of their rut and drives them to do something \u2014 that's Glamour. That's why the Seelie and Unseelie Courts are both equal in the eyes of the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:47:52-08:00","id":1034084,"title":"","content":"Does the Unseelie's affinity for &quot;bad&quot; emotions link them to the Nightmare Realms or are those Realms the dominion of the fomorian and their descendants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:15:45-08:00","id":1034102,"title":"","content":"Nightmare was once used somewhat interchangeably with the Unseelie Court, but the term is taking on a specific meaning in C20. It should help clarify some things that got a bit muddled as more and more got added to the game line during its original run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  Clarity 01-18-2017, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:34:05-08:00","id":1034110,"title":"","content":"is there a relation between the Fomori (Werewolf) and the Fomor ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:49:35-08:00","id":1034114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034110#post1034110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there a relation between the Fomori (Werewolf) and the Fomor ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891439-the-black-fomorian-dream?p=969951#post969951\">The Fomorians are the ancient primordial rulers of the world with immeasurable power imprisoned for all eternity by the Tuatha de Daanan. Fomori are some random dudes possessed by a minor spirit and easily torn to shreds by werewolves.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:58:07-08:00","id":1034117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034114#post1034114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891439-the-black-fomorian-dream?p=969951#post969951\">The Fomorians are the ancient primordial rulers of the world with immeasurable power imprisoned for all eternity by the Tuatha de Daanan. Fomori are some random dudes possessed by a minor spirit and easily torn to shreds by werewolves.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The fomorians have their own changelings followers like the adhennne and the than thallaain correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:03:00-08:00","id":1034120,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. The Adhene are composed of those fae who sided with the Fomorians during the War of Trees. The Thallain are children of the Fomorians just as the Kithain are the heirs to the Tuatha de Danaan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:52:48-08:00","id":1034261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034120#post1034120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much. The Adhene are composed of those fae who sided with the Fomorians during the War of Trees. The Thallain are children of the Fomorians just as the Kithain are the heirs to the Tuatha de Danaan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they defined by their origins or can we have Adhene and Thallain who try to be decent people? On a similar note, What about Redcaps, are they still just as hated as thallain even if they're not, how hard is for aredcap to have friends among the kithain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:29:43-08:00","id":1034287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034261#post1034261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they defined by their origins or can we have Adhene and Thallain who try to be decent people? On a similar note, What about Redcaps, are they still just as hated as thallain even if they're not, how hard is for aredcap to have friends among the kithain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Redcaps are not as hated as Thallain. They're a Kithain kith, they belong to the Dreaming, and are not considered &quot;outcast&quot; or &quot;evil&quot; in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:23:25-08:00","id":1034342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034261#post1034261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they defined by their origins or can we have Adhene and Thallain who try to be decent people? On a similar note, What about Redcaps, are they still just as hated as thallain even if they're not, how hard is for aredcap to have friends among the kithain?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Adhene only recently found their way back to Earth. They made a choice once. With Earth and the Dreaming in the shape they're in, they'll have to make more choices soon.<br /> <br /> The Thallain.... a few individuals might give weight to their secondary legacies temporarily, but the Kithain would be wise not to trust them for long. They're truly products of the Fomorian Dream.<br /> <br /> Redcaps are Kithain. They're difficult to get along with, but as Maggie says, they're no more hated as a kith than pooka, piskies, or sidhe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:48:21-08:00","id":1034670,"title":"","content":"I have another one: what is the difference between an Adhene and a Thallain?<br /> After all, they both are fae who sided with the Fomorian, right ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:02:43-08:00","id":1034678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034342#post1034342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Adhene only recently found their way back to Earth. They made a choice once. With Earth and the Dreaming in the shape they're in, they'll have to make more choices soon.<br /> <br /> The Thallain.... a few individuals might give weight to their secondary legacies temporarily, but the Kithain would be wise not to trust them for long. They're truly products of the Fomorian Dream.<br /> <br /> Redcaps are Kithain. They're difficult to get along with, but as Maggie says, they're no more hated as a kith than pooka, piskies, or sidhe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on, does that mean Thallain no longer have two Unseelie legacies? Or do you just mean that one of those legacies might be slightly better than the other? The former makes sense if we're moving away from Unseelie = evil, which always blurred things between Thallain and the Unseelie, and indeed between all fae and the Fomorians (if they're all partly evil).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:05:19-08:00","id":1034682,"title":"","content":"Check it out \u2014 a few posts above this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034120#post1034120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Adhene are composed of those fae who sided with the Fomorians during the War of Trees. The Thallain are children of the Fomorians just as the Kithain are the heirs to the Tuatha de Danaan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, there's a bit more to it than that, but C20 will be along soon-ish <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:08:21-08:00","id":1034684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034678#post1034678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hang on, does that mean Thallain no longer have two Unseelie legacies? Or do you just mean that one of those legacies might be slightly better than the other? The former makes sense if we're moving away from Unseelie = evil, which always blurred things between Thallain and the Unseelie, and indeed between all fae and the Fomorians (if they're all partly evil).</div> </div> </div> </div>^_____________^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T10:20:31-08:00","id":1034690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1034684#post1034684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ^_____________^</div> </div> </div> </div>Tease! <br /> <br /> One day soon we'll know all these answers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:03:59-08:00","id":1034726,"title":"","content":"Oh, he's so mean, isn't he? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:17:46-08:00","id":1035231,"title":"","content":"im a bit confused here. So, if a PC has Nightmare dices, they are added to the cantrip roll as if they were &quot;bonuses&quot; for the roll but with horrible consequences? or i just have to roll them and not count them as part of the main cantrip roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T03:42:54-08:00","id":1035672,"title":"","content":"Some of their dicepool are Nightmare dice. Like, you have pool of six. And one Nightmare die. Roll it separately or use a different colour, but if it fumbles you're in trouble. But it isn't bonus die, you still have a pool six. If you only left with one die (due to wounds) this is the Nightmare die.<br /> <br /> Also, on a separate note. I would love to see updated &quot;Storyteller's Guide&quot; for c20. Those books were always fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-21-2017, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T03:59:54-08:00","id":1035673,"title":"","content":"It's like Shadow dice in Wraith. They add to your dice pool, but any 1s rolled have severe consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T06:53:11-08:00","id":1035697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1035673#post1035673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like Shadow dice in Wraith. They add to your dice pool, but any 1s rolled have severe consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5211_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5211\" data-vbnamecard=\"5211\">Firkraag</a> is correct on this. They don't add to your dice pool. They replace dice in your dice pool. It's an interesting mechanic that none of the other game lines did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:38:40-08:00","id":1040182,"title":"","content":"Now, that I think of it, what are the Technocracy's opinions on Mists. Considering, that changelings and chimera are real (as another group of reality deviant, but anyway), and something <i><b>had to</b></i> corrupt and erase their surveillance data (If mages can, Technocracy, should have a tech to breach though the Mists).<br /> <br /> If anything, Mists should be considered a powerful memetic virus, working on every sentient entity, that isn't part of that select group of reality deviants.<br /> <br /> Would they want Mists removed and see a reality for what it is? Or hijack it and have such a tool for themselves, filtering, what can or can't be remembered or even seen? <br /> <br /> Could they succed at interacting with Mists at all and how it might backfire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:56:39-08:00","id":1040199,"title":"","content":"The Technocrats (Banality 8-10) are more vulnerable to the Mists than normal Mages (Banality 2-8). I doubt that many of them can even remember anything occurred other than as an accident or an equipment glitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:14:03-08:00","id":1040210,"title":"","content":"Magic, duh.<br /> <br /> I mean, I doubt, they can <i>observe</i> changelings and chimera, as &quot;fairy&quot;, etc., but they should at least register it <i>somehow</i> with Dimensional Science or Mind, when they're up to task. One glitch is one case, ignoring a systemic malfunctions with predictable patterns (<i>'infested'</i> individuals meeting and participating in <i>'mock'</i> battles; psychiatrists, collecting multiple accounts of 'collective delusion' across the country, etc.) is inexcusable mistake.<br /> <br /> They might not notice or remember these 'events' occuring, but the <i>ripples</i>? Yes! Such anomalies definitely should interest them.<br /> <br /> And technicaly, someone, like Void Engineers can 'self-enchant' themselves, as any Mage can, given a good reason within their paradigm. Other procedures might compliment it.<br /> <br /> How they interpret (their tech might show them not what a typical changeling would experience) this data might be different case entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-29-2017, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:53:07-08:00","id":1040224,"title":"","content":"Well maybe they did tried something, &amp; then the Shadow Court &amp; the Thalain noticed &amp; decided they didn't want other splats antagonists to come play on their ground, &amp; they send a bunch of Gremlins to show how a funny a paradigm relying on Technology can be.<br /> <br /> At least on a Gremlin point of view ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:58:20-08:00","id":1040227,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming and the Mists are antithetical to True Magic though. True Magic does not even work in the Deep Dreaming and the Mists react violently if anything with a Banality above 6 tries to enter the Deep Dreaming. If Technocrats attempted the circumvent the Mists, the Mists would react violently, and would probably erase the offending Mages from existence (and yes, the Mists are more powerful than any Mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:51:40-08:00","id":1040255,"title":"","content":"When I choose between distraous consequences that promote Status Quo and those, which break it, one way or another, I always choose the latter option.<br /> <br /> I just agrued with my friend about it and we came to conclusion, that for Technocracy it might mean, that Mists might work a bit <i>differently</i>. They just have enough on their plate to not investigate it. Like there might be few amalgams, that had noticed alarming signs, but they never get enough funding to investigate their claims. Yes, they detect <i>something</i>, even have som\u0443 statistics on their hands, but vampires and werewolves are more tangible and even considering, that there is no conspiracy, relatively harmless breed of reality deviants not a high priority. Not, that they won't turn their eye on them once they'll deal with other issues, that day doesn't seem to be close.<br /> <br /> We even discussed an idea of cabal of ex-technocracy operatives, who were tasked to deal with whatever threat Mists(they didn't knew, what it is, just a &quot;memetic virus&quot; of some sort) posed, which they have decided, was so great, that they went rogue and came up with a procedure to 'enchant' themselves and waged a crusade on these alien infiltrators. And how that experience changed them. They might still think they fighting a war in a middle of hostile environment, but act a lot like other supernatural groups, a lot like, changelings themselves. Maybe, even their magic is changed to reflect that, maybe even slowly turning into Maradeur...<br /> <br /> That said, consider one more thing.<br /> <br /> Despite Mists, fae are known player. Not widely known among younger generations, but there are supernatural powers (Vampire, Werefolf, Wraith, Mage), that let others interact and detect them and those powers are not affected by Mists.<br /> <br /> Any vampire with Auspex can see fae among other people. They don't know they're fae, unless they have Occult high enough, but the difference is still there. Vampires can prey on changelings if they want, and changelings couldn't hide without assistance of Arts.<br /> <br /> To consider, that Technocracy woulnd't be able to do something similar, at least, would be unreasonable. The question is how much they can do or care about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-29-2017, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:06:38-08:00","id":1040262,"title":"","content":"Well, they would then be highly vulnerable to chimerical damage and, considering that there are potentially billions of sapient chimera in the Flesh Realm (because there are billions of Dreamers), they are really outnumbered. It would be amusing though to have a Technocrat be trampled into a coma by a herd of chimerical unicorns. Their peers in the Union would also be thinking that they had cracked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-29-2017, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:51:54-08:00","id":1040291,"title":"","content":"Most supernaturals consider the Fae extinct and long gone. The Technocracy especially suffers from this misconception, because the Mists work on them near 100%.<br /> <br /> So no, I don't agree that the Technocracy can come up with a method to detect the Fae (in any meaningful way). Even if they managed it, the Mists would erase the memory of any interaction in short order so they would be left with the conclusion that they failed or that such creatures aren't really there. Same result either way. They give up trying to look for imaginary (literally) monsters.<br /> <br /> And actually thinking about it, Vampires would be hard pressed to find Fae too. Sure, you can get an obsessive one with Auspex looking at every person that walks by. What are the chances that said Vampire is going to actually know what &quot;rainbow highlights&quot; in an Aura means? If they do confront the person to find out, the Mists will roll in and wipe/alter that memory. They too would be hard pressed to actually figure out anything going on with the Changelings because of that.<br /> <br /> Out of all of the games, Changelings by far has the strongest ability to hide in plain sight. There is literally no stat you can invest in to protect yourself from the Mists. At least in the other main 4 you can have a high Willpower and be somewhat guarded against the mental manipulations of memory wipes. Not so much in Changeling.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also disagree on the idea that it's easy for Mages to &quot;self-enchant&quot;. Very few paradigms mesh well with the concept. It's been a long time since I had this disagreement with one of my friends, but from memory only the Dreamspeakers had a Rote to do so (that very well may have changed in these last several years).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:36:28-08:00","id":1040346,"title":"","content":"Kiiind of a silly question..what happends if a kithain mates and has a child with a human? and what happends when two kithains have a kid?. would a new &quot;Kith&quot; be created into existance in the case of 2 kiths going jiggy with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:48:24-08:00","id":1040352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040346#post1040346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiiind of a silly question..what happends if a kithain mates and has a child with a human? and what happends when two kithains have a kid?. would a new &quot;Kith&quot; be created into existance in the case of 2 kiths going jiggy with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiths aren't a DNA sort of thing. It doesn't work like that.<br /> <br /> Story-wise, children of Changelings seem to have a better chance at being born Changelings, but there is no guarantee that a fae soul will connect itself to the newly born human. Per &quot;new Kiths&quot;, I would say no, that's not how it works at all. However, I believe C20 is going to have a section on creating Kiths, so we will see what it says in there when the book comes out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:50:54-08:00","id":1040355,"title":"","content":"How about Changelings being one of the most numerous group of supernaturals (it's more probable to bump accidentally into any changeling, rather than a member of specific vampire clan)?<br /> <br /> Learning about &quot;rainbow highlights&quot; isn't that hard really. You just go to one of the old and versed in Occult vampires and ask. It's not like vampires are forbidden from collecting and sharing vast fonts of knowledge. That information might cost you, though, but it isn't beyond realms of possible and even plausible. Not having Auspex and not asking questions about what you can see with it is a real limit. But who have Auspex, anyway? Majority of Tremere have strong arcane backgrounds, so they at the very least, heard something about fae. Malkavians are immune to Mists, in addition to Auspex, and not all of them are complete nutjobs. Toreador might be the only clan of vampires, who are more blind the more they see. Tzimisce are... well, Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Fianna interact with fae. Gets of Fenris hate fae. Malkavians interact with fae. Kyasid are fairy-blooded vampires. Mages can do anything, as long as it doesn't conflict with their paradigm.<br /> <br /> Only Dreamspeakers have such Rote as something mandatory. I mean, it comes with the title. Or do you think, if there's no published Rote to do something, this effect is not possible or that other Tradition or Craft can't do something different?That Sons of Ether can't cook up a theory and machine to interact with fairies? That Virtual Adepts can't ever be interested in dreams? Or that Order of Hermes don't have just a spell for this (not, that all of them know it, but dragons and fairiy dust is their life and blood)? That Verbena doesn't treat as sacred the very same places, Inanimae call their home and these two never interact with each other? That's from the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Technocratic paradigm is progress of humanity and getting rid of supernatural scum, that pollutes the Earth. Detecting crazy weird shit and blasting it anti-weird-shit cannons is what they do. Void Engineers, at the very least. I mean, think of it. Visor, that shows hazy alien shapes and gooey overlay, that covers certain places - a parasitic extradimensional lifeform, that feeds off of emotions and memories. And a gun, that shoots streams of pure banality and makes place dead to Glamour! Of course, they'd call it a dimension phase interlocker or something, but chimera would weep in agony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-29-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:53:56-08:00","id":1040359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040346#post1040346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiiind of a silly question..what happends if a kithain mates and has a child with a human?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040352#post1040352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Story-wise, children of Changelings seem to have a better chance at being born Changelings</div> </div> </div> </div>And kinain. Humans with faerie blood. See &quot;The Enchanted&quot; book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-29-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:00:55-08:00","id":1040450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040355#post1040355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fianna interact with fae. Gets of Fenris hate fae. Malkavians interact with fae. Kyasid are fairy-blooded vampires. Mages can do anything, as long as it doesn't conflict with their paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fianna do interact with them, and still have no idea just how many Changelings there are. Get hate fae? well that's certainly overstated. The Get/Fae relationship is painted entirely differently from both lines. Malkavians have zero meaningful interaction with the Fae (there is an early edition Obfuscate 8 power and a throwaway fluff line somewhere that says they are immune to the Mists for no reason). There are how many Kyasid? And their backstory is beyond any sort of sense. And you really think more of Mages than I do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040355#post1040355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only Dreamspeakers have such Rote as something mandatory. I mean, it comes with the title.</div> </div> </div> </div>The title means literally nothing. Dreamspeakers specialize in interacting with Spirits. Not the Dreaming. And in fact, their revised book seems to step back the ties with the Changelings they had in previous editions. So there is that.<br /> Either way though, my bigger problem is with your assumption on how the Technocracy can interact with Changelings, so I'll skip over this and go there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040355#post1040355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocratic paradigm is progress of humanity and getting rid of supernatural scum, that pollutes the Earth. Detecting crazy weird shit and blasting it anti-weird-shit cannons is what they do. Void Engineers, at the very least. I mean, think of it. Visor, that shows hazy alien shapes and gooey overlay, that covers certain places - a parasitic extradimensional lifeform, that feeds off of emotions and memories. And a gun, that shoots streams of pure banality and makes place dead to Glamour! Of course, they'd call it a dimension phase interlocker or something, but chimera would weep in agony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having Banality ratings of 8-10 means they literally can't remember chimerical things after they've seen them. There is nothing they can do about that. That's how the Mists work in Changeling. So trying to work on a way to fight something you keep forgetting completely is kind of useless. They won't be shooting banality, because banality is quasi-disbelief (it's layered and more complicated than that). You'd have to come up with a gun concept that shoots boring tedious thoughts made solid (maybe?). And you'd have no idea why you were even trying to build it. They wouldn't call it anything, because the Technocracy as a whole doesn't believe faeries exist (which makes sense, given their Banality).<br /> So this is really my sticking point. How do you expect the Technocracy to prepare to fight an enemy they can't (literally can't) remember?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:00:35-08:00","id":1040563,"title":"","content":"There is entire Book of Lost Dreams paragraph, stating, that Malkavians are immune to Mists. And it's canon until it is revised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040450#post1040450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, we understand how our world works very differently and apply that understanding of our world to the WoD, which admittedly, is known for defying even common sense at many points, let alone laws of physics. <br /> <br /> So, I won't try to convince you.<br /> <br /> Let me rephrase. In my world of darkness Technocracy should be able to interact with changelings and chimera, though indirect means, such as memetic analys and statistics, they should have exactly the right tech to determine whether their memory was modified, when and by whom, they can spot inconsistencies in stories and get of everything, other than what they see as fact. They don't have to believe in fairies to know, that certain places are affected by extradimensional entities, that cause nightmares. They don't have to believe in fairies to see, that something corrupts their camera feeds. <br /> <br /> And they definitely don't have to believe in fairies to apply countermeasures, as long as said countermeasures work. <br /> <br /> I also find plausible, that with all of that fantastic tech and resourses changelings are so low on their list of priorities, that they didn't got to effectively implement such detectors and countermeasures. In their catalogue of anomalies none of these phenomena stirred the strings so strongly, so that their higher up would start to act. Maybe, they don't have resources. Time, personell, money and working place. Maybe, they are more interested in other research. Or maybe, that's Mists at work, changing not how they see the chimaric phenomena, but how it's treated (I can deal with it later).<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's my opinion. In your world of darkness Technocracy might cobble together some gears and coconuts with a duct tape and call it the TECHNOLOGY, for all I care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-30-2017, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:57:10-08:00","id":1040666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040563#post1040563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is entire Book of Lost Dreams paragraph, stating, that Malkavians are immune to Mists. And it's canon until it is revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, and I'm not disputing that they are. Just that, to my knowledge, nothing of substance was ever done with it. There are more than a couple of groups that have much closer ties to the Fae/Changelings that aren't immune to the Mists and so this always seemed like a waste. I don't really understand why it was set up like that and have nothing done with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040563#post1040563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, we understand how our world works very differently and apply that understanding of our world to the WoD, which admittedly, is known for defying even common sense at many points, let alone laws of physics.<br /> <br /> So, I won't try to convince you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. The WoD is written vaguely enough that there are lots of spots where things are left open. We all enjoy the setting/games for different reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-30-2017, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:53:46-08:00","id":1040698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040666#post1040666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I'm not disputing that they are. Just that, to my knowledge, nothing of substance was ever done with it. There are more than a couple of groups that have much closer ties to the Fae/Changelings that aren't immune to the Mists and so this always seemed like a waste. I don't really understand why it was set up like that and have nothing done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might br just plot hooks. A little ingredients that may be either used or ignored by particular Storyteller in a recipe of World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I mean, I've seen almost as many interpretations of Malkavian clan, as Storytellers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:08:53-08:00","id":1040702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040666#post1040666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I'm not disputing that they are. Just that, to my knowledge, nothing of substance was ever done with it. There are more than a couple of groups that have much closer ties to the Fae/Changelings that aren't immune to the Mists and so this always seemed like a waste. I don't really understand why it was set up like that and have nothing done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a crossover they were pushing harder in second edition and then broke away from in Revised. They didn't really contradict the old material, but they generally ignored it. <br /> <br /> I love Malkavians, and I love Changeling, but personally I want them far far away from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:36:53-08:00","id":1040754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040563#post1040563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is entire Book of Lost Dreams paragraph, stating, that Malkavians are immune to Mists. And it's canon until it is revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let me rephrase. In my world of darkness Technocracy should be able to interact with changelings and chimera, though indirect means, such as memetic analys and statistics, they should have exactly the right tech to determine whether their memory was modified, when and by whom, they can spot inconsistencies in stories and get of everything, other than what they see as fact. They don't have to believe in fairies to know, that certain places are affected by extradimensional entities, that cause nightmares. They don't have to believe in fairies to see, that something corrupts their camera feeds.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>From someone who actually does memetic and statistical analysis, I cannot think of any way that the Technocracy could possibly detect Changelings as Changelings or the Mists as the Mists. Memetic analysis concerns the analysis of memes and statistical analysis concerns the analysis of data. Memes are cultural units of information, so I really do not see how the Technocracy could possible use memetic analysis to find Changelings (at best, they could only use memetic analysis to find mortals who are being encouraged to be creative by Changelings). Data is information that is collected and, if you cannot remember what you are collecting, the data becomes really hard to collect, so statistical analysis would be useless because no direct data is being reported.<br /> <br /> Now, I agree that the Technocracy will notice something, but they will never be able to predict the actions of the creatures of the Dreaming because they are blind to the possibility of the Dreaming. They will probably the actions of the creatures of the Dreaming on Marauders, as the effects of Marauder Quiets and the effects of the Mists have enough similarities that the Technocracy would ignore any anomalies as noise in the data. When the Technocracy notices the actions of the creatures of the Dreaming, they will probably send in their Marauder Clean Up teams to deal with the area (altering mortal memories further) and will never suspect that they are dealing with the Dreaming. After all, the Union be much more likely to accept a Marauder attack as an explanation than a Faerie attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:44:28-08:00","id":1040794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040702#post1040702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a crossover they were pushing harder in second edition and then broke away from in Revised. They didn't really contradict the old material, but they generally ignored it.<br /> <br /> I love Malkavians, and I love Changeling, but personally I want them far far away from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've used it for crossover before. Worked out well enough for a singular Malkavian Elder. I don't think having the whole Clan in on it would work as well story-wise.<br /> <br /> Either way, in the scope of the WoD this connection was entirely ignored for the better part of the game's runs. Fianna don't have any sort of immunity but were written with a Changeling connection in mind. Same for Sluagh and Wraiths. Hell, the writers seemed to have put more effort into a Gangrel-Garou connection (which doesn't make much sense either) than they did in the Malkavian-Changeling one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:04:53-08:00","id":1040829,"title":"","content":"Malkavians is one of the more inconsistent clans. And one of the more diverse. I treat it as, there are clan members, who use that connection (for fun and profit) and the ones, who completely ignore it (sometimes, as if it doesn't exist). Some Malkavians may have some sort of mystical wisdom, that lets them look beyond other's paradigms and see the world for what it is, while others are just undead people with mental illness. Some are connected to the Malkavian Madness Network and some never heard about it. And basically anything inbetween.<br /> <br /> There's even bunch of awesome traits to reflect that. <br /> <br /> There are some common themes, realted to clan, but no obligation to follow them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:42:31-08:00","id":1040865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040829#post1040829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malkavians is one of the more inconsistent clans. And one of the more diverse. I treat it as, there are clan members, who use that connection (for fun and profit) and the ones, who completely ignore it (sometimes, as if it doesn't exist). Some Malkavians may have some sort of mystical wisdom, that lets them look beyond other's paradigms and see the world for what it is, while others are just undead people with mental illness. Some are connected to the Malkavian Madness Network and some never heard about it. And basically anything inbetween.<br /> <br /> There's even bunch of awesome traits to reflect that.<br /> <br /> There are some common themes, realted to clan, but no obligation to follow them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Though system-wise I think it would be better represented as a Merit then. Something in the Clan book that would point to a connection that players can take or not. It shouldn't be something every Clan member has, because if that's the case then Changelings would be much more important to the Clan.<br /> <br /> Having access (even if it's only knowing where to start) to Changelings (or any Supernatural group; i.e. see the Giovanni) is a huge potential resource for a Vampire Clan. It would have played a much bigger part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:51:44-08:00","id":1040873,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly (and it is quite possible that I'm wrong), I believe that some of the books said that those that were mad could often see things of the Dreaming, and that the Malkavian ability to see changelings rested on the fact that they were all insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:54:33-08:00","id":1040874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040873#post1040873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly (and it is quite possible that I'm wrong), I believe that some of the books said that those that were mad could often see things of the Dreaming, and that the Malkavian ability to see changelings rested on the fact that they were all insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, &quot;the Mad&quot; had a lower Banality rating. So did drunkards. Either way though, it seems like a missed opportunity to not actually go anywhere with it for the Malkavians as long as they were putting that rule in there to begin with. I usually just choose to scrap it entirely if I don't need it for a particular story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:12:31-08:00","id":1040885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040874#post1040874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, &quot;the Mad&quot; had a lower Banality rating. So did drunkards. Either way though, it seems like a missed opportunity to not actually go anywhere with it for the Malkavians as long as they were putting that rule in there to begin with. I usually just choose to scrap it entirely if I don't need it for a particular story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now i'm imagining a changeling staving off being undone by being perpetually, Sterling Archer-level drunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:29:18-08:00","id":1040897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040874#post1040874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So did drunkards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always ignored that part.<br /> <br /> Knew a fair share of drunkards in my neighbourhood, when I was a kid. It feels, like opposite of Dreaming. All life and happiness is sucked out of people and their living space. Despair is slowly creeps on you from every corner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 01-30-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:07:27-08:00","id":1040930,"title":"","content":"We tend to notice depressing or mean drunks more than happy or whimsical drunks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:22:04-08:00","id":1040939,"title":"","content":"&quot;Happy and whimsical&quot; drunks (if we mean cases of alcoholism, not &quot;occasional&quot; drinkers) still show various stages of mental and physical degradation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:41:48-08:00","id":1040994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040874#post1040874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, &quot;the Mad&quot; had a lower Banality rating. So did drunkards. Either way though, it seems like a missed opportunity to not actually go anywhere with it for the Malkavians as long as they were putting that rule in there to begin with. I usually just choose to scrap it entirely if I don't need it for a particular story.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Book of Lost Dreams, p. 12, it states that Malkavians are immune to the Mists (probably due to their insanity), so the Malkavians remember everything. Potentially, Malkavians could be enchanted, dragged into the Deep Dreaming, and remember everything that happens (even more than the Changelings themselves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T20:00:54-08:00","id":1041069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040885#post1040885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now i'm imagining a changeling staving off being undone by being perpetually, Sterling Archer-level drunk.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most of the my games substance abuse is a pretty common coping mechanism for Changelings in the downward spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T20:24:04-08:00","id":1041079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1040994#post1040994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Book of Lost Dreams, p. 12, it states that Malkavians are immune to the Mists (probably due to their insanity), so the Malkavians remember everything. Potentially, Malkavians could be enchanted, dragged into the Deep Dreaming, and remember everything that happens (even more than the Changelings themselves).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the rule. That doesn't make it any less dumb or make any more sense. And it's made all the more dumb by them never doing anything with it anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:19:42-08:00","id":1045419,"title":"","content":"Does Boggan's Birthright helps to do your taxes faster? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or is it covers only physical activities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:46:14-08:00","id":1045887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1045419#post1045419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Boggan's Birthright helps to do your taxes faster? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or is it covers only physical activities?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to be physical labour. However, if they're just flicking through papers and pushing keys on a calculator, you could argue that's mostly physical. If the boggan has to do maths in their head, then it would be a definite no. The reading might tip the balance, but even building requires thought and planning, so it's Storyteller's call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:52:10-08:00","id":1045892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1045419#post1045419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Does Boggan's Birthright helps to do your taxes faster? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or is it covers only physical activities?</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely seems outside of the intent of their Birthright, but I don't think I would have a problem with it if a player really wanted to use it to do taxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:46:16-08:00","id":1045971,"title":"","content":"I would say it depends on how they're doing their taxes, how extensive they are, and what parts. Example, I would consider filling out reams of paperwork or performing large amounts of data entry to be within the realm of their Birthright, but not doing math problems. Taxes are kind of a little of both. So if they're mostly just ticking the boxes and scratching the totals, then sure I'd say their Birthright applies. For the mental part of it though, performing the calculations and navigating the different tax codes, their Birthright wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T17:49:36-08:00","id":1046085,"title":"","content":"So, what about cooking dishes, then?<br /> <br /> Birthright doesn't cover the mental part, as well? Therefore, doesn't cover cooking at all, as mentals component of culinary seem to be inseparable from physical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 02-08-2017, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:04:48-08:00","id":1046092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1046085#post1046085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what about cooking dishes, then?<br /> <br /> Birthright doesn't cover the mental part, as well? Therefore, doesn't cover cooking at all, as mentals component of culinary seem to be inseparable from physical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cooking should fall under the Birthright","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T02:03:25-08:00","id":1046217,"title":"","content":"You have to think of the spirit of the thing. The birthright is supposed to cover fairy tales like the elves who help the shoemaker, and Rumpelstiltskin. They do things around the house/workplace. Chores and domestic work.<br /> <br /> Cooking definitely falls into that category. Depending on your worldview, doing household taxes might too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:15:38-08:00","id":1046849,"title":"","content":"Now, that we have kith maker, I was thinking... Maybe chimera changelings are possible? They're less chimeric and more anthropomorphic, but should it be at all possible for a particularly strong chimera (4+) to follow Changeling Way?<br /> <br /> Also, are there a written/known instances the ritual of Changeling Way or was it just a plot device of Sundering times?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:34:57-08:00","id":1046860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1046849#post1046849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe chimera changelings are possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote a thing in C20 specifically to answer this question since it's been a common one over the years. <i>Hypothetically</i>, the chimera wouldn't be able to become a changeling directly. It would need to somehow make the leap from chimera to Kithain before it could undergo the Changeling Way. Chimera, even extremely powerful ones, just aren't as tangible as Kithain or other fae, metaphysically speaking.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T12:28:55-08:00","id":1046882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1046860#post1046860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would need to somehow make the leap from chimera to Kithain before it could undergo the Changeling Way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic?<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> </span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:06:27-08:00","id":1046893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1046860#post1046860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wrote a thing in C20 specifically to answer this question since it's been a common one over the years. <i>Hypothetically</i>, the chimera wouldn't be able to become a changeling directly. It would need to somehow make the leap from chimera to Kithain before it could undergo the Changeling Way. Chimera, even extremely powerful ones, just aren't as tangible as Kithain or other fae, metaphysically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>All that in mind, I'd say that for a chimera to make that leap, they'd need to have a strong motivation to change what they are. Your average chimera is probably pretty content, so for it to start a new kith, it would probably need to be pretty desperate. I'm sure that it's probably happened at least once. Maybe even more than once...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:45:45-08:00","id":1046908,"title":"","content":"I think that the creation of a new Kith would be a once in a century event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T19:56:28-08:00","id":1047031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1046860#post1046860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wrote a thing in C20 specifically to answer this question since it's been a common one over the years. <i>Hypothetically</i>, the chimera wouldn't be able to become a changeling directly. It would need to somehow make the leap from chimera to Kithain before it could undergo the Changeling Way. Chimera, even extremely powerful ones, just aren't as tangible as Kithain or other fae, metaphysically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of a weird hypothetical jumping off the same general precipice. Could it be theoretically possible for a Kinain to have a chimerical parent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T20:05:38-08:00","id":1047035,"title":"","content":"I would say no, but if it works for your game, don't let me stop you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:52:20-08:00","id":1049078,"title":"","content":"i been binge reading The Sandman and Neverwhere. and i finished the corebook (im starting the player's guide and waiting to find Denizents of the dreaming)<br /> <br /> But...im a bit confused on one thing, im fascinated by The Corinthian from The Sandman, but would he be a Chimera or would he be a Kith or a Fomor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Fo