l image looks. i meant when having the full collection of books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T23:40:25-07:00","id":1081730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1081638#post1081638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, i noticed some books have art on the side..how does the final image looks. i meant when having the full collection of books?</div> </div> </div> </div>The line finished before the picture could be completed; IIRC, the final picture would have been a combination of the covers to the three Immortal Eyes sourcebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T03:13:59-07:00","id":1082550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032392#post1032392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, chimeras without Wyrd and Enchantment redes, could they interact with inanimate object of Autumn World? Open and close doors, steal things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a chimera can interact with the mundane/ Autumn world (and indeed has to): a closed door is a closed door and the chimera must open it to get through (or destroy it). However, when surrounded by non-enchanted people, chimera are on the other side of the Mists (because of the witnesses' Banality) and so cannot interact with the mundane world. This is why chimera often stalk their changeling prey, waiting for the moment when they will be alone...<br /> <br /> So, the Monster Under the Bed waits for the childling's parent to leave in order to open the door of the wardrobe in which it was hiding...<br /> <br /> Also, remember that if a non-enchanted witness sees a real-world effect by a chimera (a changeling riding a horse and thus apparently floating), her disbelief will shunt the Kithain into a random part of the Dreaming unless the chimera (and only if she is sentient) succeeds a Willpower roll against the witness's Banality.<br /> <br /> Finally, when a chimera is near a non-enchanted people whose Banality is 2 or more than her Glamour rating, it suffers one Level of Health every turn. So, for instance, a chimera with Glamour 5 is near a human near a Banality of 7, the chimera suffers one Health Level every turn, prompting the chimera to quickly go elsewhere. This is why chimera avoid areas with Banal people. (Changeling: the Dreaming, 2nd ed., p. 224a)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 04-23-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T03:20:24-07:00","id":1082551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1032923#post1032923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Art of Spring ? Jeez... I eager for the release of C20.<br /> <br /> I have a question about something I have trouble to understand in the rulebook. It's about Enchantment and the difficulty of cantrips on mortals. I've seen at several place in the book that Enchanting a mortal helps a Changeling to cast cantrip on him because he had already circumvent his Banality. But nowhere in the Enchantment or Arts rules I've seen something close to that statement.<br /> Is it that the Banality of the mortal is dropping when I enchant him or am I missing something? The first possibility makes sense but I don't remember seeing anything about a drop of the Banality rate in the rule on Enchantment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enchanting someone helps casting cantrips on her because, according to the rules of 2nd ed., then cantrips cast on her by a changeling will be Chimerical (not Wyrd), and will not necessarily call for a Glamour expenditure. Also, if you apply an optional rule, enchanted targets are at Banality +4 as target difficulty (before performing a Bunk) while non-enchanted targets are at Banality +5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T03:32:23-07:00","id":1082552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1081730#post1081730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The line finished before the picture could be completed; IIRC, the final picture would have been a combination of the covers to the three Immortal Eyes sourcebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check that, misremembered. The spine picture was an Immortal Eyes picture, <a href=\"https://scontent.flhr4-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t31.0-8/10633625_558450637594147_693084525654759095_o.jpg?oh=0c0f270afab22f959d0e06747c56ab39&amp;oe=598AE153\" target=\"_blank\">but it looked like this</a> (courtesy of the C20 Facebook page).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T03:35:03-07:00","id":1082554,"title":"","content":"The final spine image:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.oocities.org/pookaplace/books/spine.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.oocities.org/images/titleline.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oocities.org/pookaplace/books/spine.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oocities.org/pookaplace/books/spine.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.oocities.org/pookaplace/books/spine.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Pooka Place - Published and recommended books and material for Changeling: The Dreaming </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T06:06:50-07:00","id":1082570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1082550#post1082550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, a chimera can interact with the mundane/ Autumn world (and indeed has to): a closed door is a closed door and the chimera must open it to get through (or destroy it). However, when surrounded by non-enchanted people, chimera are on the other side of the Mists (because of the witnesses' Banality) and so cannot interact with the mundane world. This is why chimera often stalk their changeling prey, waiting for the moment when they will be alone...<br /> <br /> So, the Monster Under the Bed waits for the childling's parent to leave in order to open the door of the wardrobe in which it was hiding...<br /> <br /> Also, remember that if a non-enchanted witness sees a real-world effect by a chimera (a changeling riding a horse and thus apparently floating), her disbelief will shunt the Kithain into a random part of the Dreaming unless the chimera (and only if she is sentient) succeeds a Willpower roll against the witness's Banality.<br /> <br /> Fnally, when a chimera is near a non-enchanted people whose Banality is 2 or more than her Glamour rating, it suffers one Level of Health every turn. So, for instance, a chimera with Glamour 5 is near a human near a Banality of 7, the chimera suffers one Health Level every turn, prompting the chimera to quickly go elsewhere. This is why chimera avoid areas with Banal people. (Changeling: the Dreaming, 2nd ed., p. 224a)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hail, traveler!<br /> <br /> I like your explanation better, even if I'm not sure if it's canon (it wasn't quite clear in 2nd edition). Nevertheless, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 04-23-2017, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:52:09-07:00","id":1082635,"title":"","content":"Yes, yes, it is. Check the page I have quoted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T09:14:47-07:00","id":1082649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1082550#post1082550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, remember that if a non-enchanted witness sees a real-world effect by a chimera (a changeling riding a horse and thus apparently floating)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, the <i>Emperor's New Horse</i>, pretty much?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:29:45-07:00","id":1082789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Changeling: the Dreaming, 2nd ed., p. 224a) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1082635#post1082635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes, it is. Check the page I have quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops, I missed it, it seems!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 04-23-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:19:08-07:00","id":1082845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1082551#post1082551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enchanting someone helps casting cantrips on her because, according to the rules of 2nd ed., then cantrips cast on her by a changeling will be Chimerical (not Wyrd), and will not necessarily call for a Glamour expenditure. Also, if you apply an optional rule, enchanted targets are at Banality +4 as target difficulty (before performing a Bunk) while non-enchanted targets are at Banality +5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thanks. Ok, I understand it better know, I haven't connected the dots, it makes sense. I don't remember the rule about the Banality +4 on enchanted people, is it in the corebook ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:38:52-07:00","id":1089178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1082845#post1082845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh thanks. Ok, I understand it better know, I haven't connected the dots, it makes sense. I don't remember the rule about the Banality +4 on enchanted people, is it in the corebook ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is: p. 205b. But I don't remember were the optional rule was (maybe Player's Guide).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T20:39:38-07:00","id":1098644,"title":"","content":"two questions<br /> Does the age of the Human and the Kith corelate? what i mean is. Can a little kid (5-10) be a grump? or that rarely happends?<br /> <br /> Second...Kith and Kith fuck and they have a kid, is the kid also a Kith? or Kith an Human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T21:00:57-07:00","id":1098648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1098644#post1098644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">two questions<br /> Does the age of the Human and the Kith corelate? what i mean is. Can a little kid (5-10) be a grump? or that rarely happends?<br /> <br /> Second...Kith and Kith fuck and they have a kid, is the kid also a Kith? or Kith an Human?</div> </div> </div> </div>First. Since C20 the seemings are no longer tied to age in any way so yes you could have a kid grump or an adult childing.<br /> <br /> The child of two Fae is going to be Kinain, that is Fae-blooded, with I think a better chance for acting as a Host of a reincarnating fae soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T16:40:20-07:00","id":1099682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1098648#post1098648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First. Since C20 the seemings are no longer tied to age in any way so yes you could have a kid grump or an adult childing.<br /> <br /> The child of two Fae is going to be Kinain, that is Fae-blooded, with I think a better chance for acting as a Host of a reincarnating fae soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *Might* be Kinain. The Dreaming doesn't seem to much like Punnett squares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T11:51:18-07:00","id":1100186,"title":"","content":"im curious about the Shadow Court (but the book is a bit expensive on Ebay). So...is it a Must Have? whats about, whats their deal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T23:38:18-07:00","id":1101875,"title":"","content":"Actually... pooka dinosaurs (or any of the extinct mammals)? <br /> <br /> Does that happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:58:09-07:00","id":1102079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1101875#post1101875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually... pooka dinosaurs (or any of the extinct mammals)? <br /> <br /> Does that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kithbook Pooka, p.27</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Those pooka whose animals risk extinction walk a very fine line. It has been noted that once an animal disappears from the world, the pooka related to it gradually disappear as well. Though some pooka have affinities with animals already extinct, they fear that the next time around, they won't reincarnate and will disappear as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, Dreaming is a rather inclusive realm and if your game becomes more glamorous through dinosaur pooka then go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:05:33-07:00","id":1102082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1029643-changeling-questions-from-a-newbie?p=1101875#post1101875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually... pooka dinosaurs (or any of the extinct mammals)? <br /> <br /> Does that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Puts on pooka ears) Of course it happens! All the time, in fact! Their favorite way to gain Glamour is through veloci-Rapture. (/takes off ears)<br /> <br /> Okay, I'm done now. Couldn't help myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond th